2
00:02:09,285 --> 00:02:12,850
Episode 87

3
00:03:55,085 --> 00:03:56,585
Osman Bey!

4
00:04:17,695 --> 00:04:19,755
Brother, call for help! Now!

5
00:04:21,325 --> 00:04:22,665
Allah!

6
00:04:23,025 --> 00:04:24,375
My Sheik!

7
00:04:25,865 --> 00:04:27,705
Close Söğüt!

8
00:04:27,925 --> 00:04:31,455
Don't let anyone in or out!

9
00:04:31,625 --> 00:04:33,235
No one will leave!

10
00:04:34,275 --> 00:04:35,685
No one!

11
00:04:35,825 --> 00:04:39,205
Get everyone who came to and left the
tavern!

12
00:04:39,505 --> 00:04:41,595
Don't ever return without a trace!

13
00:04:41,595 --> 00:04:42,885
Come on!

14
00:04:42,885 --> 00:04:44,255
Yes, my Bey!

15
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,655
Konur, come on!

16
00:04:45,725 --> 00:04:47,035
Brothers, come on!

17
00:04:47,095 --> 00:04:48,105
Come on!

18
00:04:56,605 --> 00:04:59,415
I hope everyone is fine, Cornelia.

19
00:05:00,025 --> 00:05:03,065
Someone obviously wants to kill Osman Bey.

20
00:05:06,285 --> 00:05:09,955
How could they explode all Söğüt just
for Osman Bey?

21
00:05:10,775 --> 00:05:12,725
Who would do this cruel act, Cornelia?

22
00:05:18,875 --> 00:05:20,065
Of course...

23
00:05:21,095 --> 00:05:22,625
...at such a time...

24
00:05:22,925 --> 00:05:26,585
...there can be no one other than Gündüz
Bey who wants to kill Osman Bey.

25
00:05:27,175 --> 00:05:29,215
What are you saying...

26
00:05:29,285 --> 00:05:30,545
...Selvi Hatun?

27
00:05:30,625 --> 00:05:32,625
Don't you know, Erdoğdu?

28
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:34,705
Söğüt exploded!

29
00:05:39,175 --> 00:05:40,915
I will go inform Malhun.

30
00:05:46,785 --> 00:05:49,355
People say Gündüz Bey exploded Söğüt.

31
00:05:49,355 --> 00:05:51,355
What are you saying, Cornelia?

32
00:05:52,385 --> 00:05:54,635
How could Gündüz Bey become such an
evil man?

33
00:05:55,475 --> 00:05:57,265
Didn't we know him at all?

34
00:05:57,265 --> 00:05:59,025
Don't, Cornelia.

35
00:05:59,105 --> 00:06:00,835
Gündüz Bey is a prisoner.

36
00:06:01,165 --> 00:06:02,875
How could he do all this?

37
00:06:03,715 --> 00:06:05,745
Someone is trapping my bey.

38
00:06:05,765 --> 00:06:07,085
Don't you see?

39
00:06:07,155 --> 00:06:09,175
It doesn't matter if I see or not.

40
00:06:09,195 --> 00:06:11,195
Everyone is talking about it.

41
00:06:12,755 --> 00:06:15,485
If Gündüz Bey can't justify himself...

42
00:06:16,735 --> 00:06:18,045
...he will die.

43
00:06:19,375 --> 00:06:21,965
How can my Bey justify himself while he
is prisoned?

44
00:06:27,795 --> 00:06:29,305
But if he runs away...

45
00:06:30,625 --> 00:06:32,645
...he can save himself.

46
00:06:33,165 --> 00:06:34,515
-Akça!
-I am fine.

47
00:06:34,515 --> 00:06:35,735
-Are you?
-I am.

48
00:06:35,735 --> 00:06:36,905
I am fine, my Bey.

49
00:06:42,285 --> 00:06:43,845
Father!

50
00:06:45,805 --> 00:06:47,125
Father!

51
00:06:48,485 --> 00:06:49,805
Father!

52
00:06:51,305 --> 00:06:53,455
Father!

53
00:06:53,825 --> 00:06:55,025
My Sheik!

54
00:06:55,105 --> 00:06:56,395
Help!

55
00:06:56,395 --> 00:06:57,915
My Sheik!

56
00:07:03,525 --> 00:07:04,875
Help!

57
00:07:04,875 --> 00:07:06,225
Come on!

58
00:07:06,565 --> 00:07:07,905
Come on!

59
00:07:10,485 --> 00:07:11,995
My Sheik!

60
00:07:12,005 --> 00:07:13,385
Father!

61
00:07:13,435 --> 00:07:15,465
My Sheik!

62
00:07:21,015 --> 00:07:23,065
They are still together.

63
00:07:23,205 --> 00:07:25,245
But it won't be long.

64
00:07:27,415 --> 00:07:28,935
Weak!

65
00:07:29,135 --> 00:07:32,265
Both his breath and his heartbeat!

66
00:07:33,695 --> 00:07:35,195
My Allah, protect him!

67
00:07:35,265 --> 00:07:36,845
My Sheik!

68
00:07:37,025 --> 00:07:39,555
-Stretcher!
-Stretcher!

69
00:07:46,875 --> 00:07:48,895
Come on, give me the stretcher!

70
00:07:49,625 --> 00:07:50,965
Come on!

71
00:07:51,705 --> 00:07:53,055
Be careful!

72
00:07:53,115 --> 00:07:55,405
Slowly! Be careful!

73
00:07:57,995 --> 00:08:00,695
It is all because of me!

74
00:08:00,695 --> 00:08:03,265
It is all because of me, my Bey!

75
00:08:03,265 --> 00:08:04,855
What did you do?

76
00:08:04,855 --> 00:08:08,205
These are the irons we put in gunpowder,
my Bey!

77
00:08:08,305 --> 00:08:09,485
My Sheik!

78
00:08:09,485 --> 00:08:11,425
They hit us with our ammunition!

79
00:08:11,575 --> 00:08:15,105
Take some alps with you, go to your tent!

80
00:08:15,165 --> 00:08:16,475
Those who did this to us...

81
00:08:16,475 --> 00:08:18,535
...may trap you there as well.
Come on!

82
00:08:18,685 --> 00:08:22,645
I hope I will come across those who
did this, my Bey!

83
00:08:33,025 --> 00:08:34,554
Don't cry, my Ayşe.

84
00:08:36,424 --> 00:08:38,174
No one shows us mercy.

85
00:08:38,905 --> 00:08:40,445
Why are you crying?

86
00:08:42,245 --> 00:08:44,265
Mari is gone, my Bey.

87
00:08:44,655 --> 00:08:46,715
With her baby.

88
00:08:47,245 --> 00:08:48,825
I can't bare it.

89
00:08:52,035 --> 00:08:53,355
My Bey!

90
00:08:56,575 --> 00:08:58,625
My Bey, someone exploded...

91
00:08:59,185 --> 00:09:00,985
...Söğüt, the tavern.

92
00:09:01,185 --> 00:09:02,925
What are you saying, Erdoğdu?

93
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:05,865
Osman?

94
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:07,195
Alps?

95
00:09:07,215 --> 00:09:09,015
Tell me!

96
00:09:09,105 --> 00:09:10,905
There are many martyrs, my Bey.

97
00:09:11,305 --> 00:09:15,025
But the people are already talking
about you, my Bey.

98
00:09:15,935 --> 00:09:18,025
they say, Gündüz Bey exploded Söğüt...

99
00:09:18,065 --> 00:09:20,585
...and tried to kill Osman Bey.

100
00:09:23,365 --> 00:09:24,905
We need to run away.

101
00:09:26,625 --> 00:09:29,485
If a leaf falls from the tree, they will
say it is me!

102
00:09:30,675 --> 00:09:32,735
Who did this, Ayşe?

103
00:09:33,725 --> 00:09:35,315
I don't know, Gündüz.

104
00:09:35,805 --> 00:09:38,525
But someone is trying to blame us.

105
00:09:38,945 --> 00:09:40,755
What will we do now?

106
00:09:44,895 --> 00:09:46,445
We will run away.

107
00:09:46,755 --> 00:09:48,825
We will run away and then justify
ourselves.

108
00:09:49,065 --> 00:09:53,155
As long as we stay in this hole, we
can't figure out who did it.

109
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:57,185
Erdoğdu, you know what to do.

110
00:09:57,185 --> 00:09:59,245
I already got the carriage ready,
my Bey.

111
00:09:59,335 --> 00:10:01,875
We have to go before the guardian Alps
come.

112
00:10:03,875 --> 00:10:05,885
It is not the right time but...

113
00:10:06,735 --> 00:10:09,295
How can we leave the tribe in the open?

114
00:10:13,445 --> 00:10:14,795
Get him up!

115
00:10:14,865 --> 00:10:17,395
Come on! Go! Go! Go!
Come on!

116
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,375
My Sheik!

117
00:10:19,375 --> 00:10:20,965
-Come on!
-Come on!

118
00:10:23,485 --> 00:10:24,845
Come on!

119
00:10:24,845 --> 00:10:26,905
Rest of you, go help people!

120
00:10:26,905 --> 00:10:28,285
Come on!

121
00:10:30,175 --> 00:10:31,675
Hang on, my Sheik!

122
00:10:31,745 --> 00:10:32,955
Hang on!

123
00:10:33,005 --> 00:10:33,825
Hang on!

124
00:10:33,825 --> 00:10:35,375
Come on!

125
00:10:35,455 --> 00:10:36,845
Come on!

126
00:10:39,155 --> 00:10:40,665
Hang on, my Sheik!

127
00:10:40,695 --> 00:10:41,875
Hang on!

128
00:10:41,875 --> 00:10:43,225
My Bey!

129
00:10:43,245 --> 00:10:44,775
My Bey! My Bey!

130
00:10:44,865 --> 00:10:46,695
We found the car on the other
street...

131
00:10:46,715 --> 00:10:48,225
...which brought the apples.

132
00:10:48,295 --> 00:10:50,305
But no one is there.

133
00:10:54,725 --> 00:10:56,265
Help!

134
00:10:57,995 --> 00:10:59,545
Take my Sheik!

135
00:10:59,995 --> 00:11:02,575
I will spoil that devil's game!

136
00:11:02,585 --> 00:11:03,915
Come on!

137
00:11:03,965 --> 00:11:05,275
Come on!

138
00:11:06,385 --> 00:11:08,175
Come on! Help!

139
00:11:49,935 --> 00:11:51,315
Trap!

140
00:11:52,505 --> 00:11:53,845
Trap!

141
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:22,925
Vile dog!

142
00:12:27,395 --> 00:12:29,205
The devil's dog!

143
00:12:29,845 --> 00:12:31,865
Their games don't end!

144
00:12:31,865 --> 00:12:33,945
I will make him talk!

145
00:12:33,945 --> 00:12:35,965
Bring him, come on!

146
00:12:35,965 --> 00:12:37,545
Yes, My Bey!

147
00:12:39,745 --> 00:12:41,115
Up! Up!

148
00:12:42,435 --> 00:12:43,795
Come on!

149
00:12:43,835 --> 00:12:45,215
Walk!

150
00:12:45,225 --> 00:12:46,555
Come on!

151
00:12:47,905 --> 00:12:49,285
Walk!

152
00:13:29,315 --> 00:13:31,325
What are you carrying, brother Erdoğdu?

153
00:13:31,385 --> 00:13:34,085
I'm taking supplies to the surrounding
villages, brother.

154
00:13:34,195 --> 00:13:36,075
Osman Bey's order.

155
00:13:36,365 --> 00:13:39,895
He wants me to complete Gündüz Bey's
duties.

156
00:13:41,365 --> 00:13:42,755
Go!

157
00:13:57,285 --> 00:13:58,805
Selvi Hatun!

158
00:14:06,085 --> 00:14:07,605
Selvi Hatun...

159
00:14:08,085 --> 00:14:11,405
...I saw something but I don't know
to whom or how to tell.

160
00:14:12,965 --> 00:14:14,205
What is it, Cornelia?

161
00:14:15,225 --> 00:14:16,605
Tell me.

162
00:14:27,985 --> 00:14:29,685
Tell me, Cornelia.

163
00:14:30,065 --> 00:14:31,585
What did you see?

164
00:14:31,965 --> 00:14:33,275
Gündüz Bey...

165
00:14:34,245 --> 00:14:36,795
...and Ayşe Hatun are running away.

166
00:14:36,885 --> 00:14:38,625
What are you saying, Cornelia?

167
00:14:38,685 --> 00:14:40,705
How can they?

168
00:14:40,845 --> 00:14:42,595
I saw them getting into the barrels.

169
00:14:44,455 --> 00:14:46,235
Erdoğdu is taking them.

170
00:14:46,825 --> 00:14:48,415
Erdoğdu!

171
00:14:50,725 --> 00:14:52,765
Do you know where they went?

172
00:14:53,235 --> 00:14:54,615
I do.

173
00:14:59,335 --> 00:15:01,335
Run! Run!

174
00:15:03,645 --> 00:15:05,655
Help me!

175
00:15:24,585 --> 00:15:26,105
Are you afraid?

176
00:15:52,825 --> 00:15:54,825
You should've been.

177
00:16:18,685 --> 00:16:20,445
Hang on, my Sheik! Hang on!

178
00:16:20,525 --> 00:16:22,065
Hang on, my Sheik!

179
00:16:23,245 --> 00:16:25,005
In the name of Allah!

180
00:16:28,745 --> 00:16:30,265
Hang on, my Sheik!

181
00:16:30,305 --> 00:16:32,085
Hang on!

182
00:16:50,385 --> 00:16:51,725
Father!

183
00:16:52,525 --> 00:16:54,255
Father! What happened?

184
00:16:54,345 --> 00:16:56,105
What happened, Kumral Abdal?

185
00:16:56,185 --> 00:16:57,565
How is he?

186
00:16:57,585 --> 00:16:59,665
Allah will heal I hope but...

187
00:17:00,305 --> 00:17:02,005
...his wounds are too deep.

188
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,385
He lost so much blood.

189
00:17:05,243 --> 00:17:07,315
We will bandage his wounds and wait.

190
00:17:09,085 --> 00:17:12,325
Hang on, father! Hang on!
Don't leave us in the dark!

191
00:17:12,355 --> 00:17:13,655
Hang on!

192
00:17:13,694 --> 00:17:15,065
Hang on!

193
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:18,095
We couldn't protect our Sheik, Bala Hatun.

194
00:17:18,585 --> 00:17:20,085
We are sorry.

195
00:17:22,185 --> 00:17:24,194
If my Sheik opened his eyes now...

196
00:17:24,365 --> 00:17:26,555
...he would tell us to
consent to the calamity.

197
00:17:26,785 --> 00:17:29,125
He would say that every cloud
has a silver lining.

198
00:17:29,125 --> 00:17:30,905
Allah knows but we don't.

199
00:17:33,015 --> 00:17:35,945
How can our hearts find healing now?

200
00:17:36,045 --> 00:17:37,425
Father!

201
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:39,565
Give me a bandage, Kumral Abdal!

202
00:17:39,585 --> 00:17:40,975
Give me a bandage!

203
00:17:41,015 --> 00:17:42,565
My Sheik!

204
00:17:43,735 --> 00:17:45,105
My Sheik!

205
00:17:45,135 --> 00:17:46,505
My Sheik!

206
00:17:46,515 --> 00:17:47,905
My Sheik!

207
00:17:49,885 --> 00:17:51,215
Bala...

208
00:17:51,215 --> 00:17:53,275
What will we do if something
happens to him?

209
00:17:55,045 --> 00:17:56,765
No. No.

210
00:17:57,085 --> 00:17:58,635
My Sheik is strong!

211
00:17:58,925 --> 00:18:00,305
He will survive!

212
00:18:01,395 --> 00:18:02,965
Kumral Abdal!

213
00:18:04,825 --> 00:18:07,085
I hope so, my Bey.
I hope so.

214
00:18:18,115 --> 00:18:19,415
Where do we go now, my Bey?

215
00:18:19,545 --> 00:18:20,915
You hide the carriage.

216
00:18:20,915 --> 00:18:22,695
There are caves nearby.

217
00:18:22,755 --> 00:18:24,485
We will spend the night there.

218
00:18:24,485 --> 00:18:26,035
All right, my Bey.

219
00:18:26,995 --> 00:18:28,525
Gündüz...

220
00:18:29,265 --> 00:18:31,275
...how will we justify ourselves?

221
00:18:32,405 --> 00:18:35,995
We will find those who betrayed us,
my Ayşe.

222
00:18:36,175 --> 00:18:37,525
Don't worry.

223
00:18:40,805 --> 00:18:42,195
My Bey!

224
00:18:42,275 --> 00:18:43,785
Someone is coming, my Bey!

225
00:18:43,785 --> 00:18:44,965
Ayşe!

226
00:18:44,965 --> 00:18:47,015
Ayşe, run! Come on!

227
00:18:48,655 --> 00:18:50,675
Where are you running to, Gündüz Bey?

228
00:18:51,375 --> 00:18:52,885
Come on, Ayşe!

229
00:18:52,975 --> 00:18:54,755
Let's get them!

230
00:19:02,305 --> 00:19:04,845
Why didn't you stay with Bala Hatun?

231
00:19:04,895 --> 00:19:07,485
There are many men there. Don't
worry, Cerkutay.

232
00:19:11,925 --> 00:19:13,425
Alps!

233
00:19:15,535 --> 00:19:17,065
Be careful.

234
00:19:38,585 --> 00:19:40,155
They destroyed it.

235
00:19:59,335 --> 00:20:03,425
Who would do this, Cerkutay?
Why?

236
00:20:04,055 --> 00:20:05,375
I don't know.

237
00:20:06,405 --> 00:20:09,405
But we will find out.

238
00:20:14,095 --> 00:20:15,825
It can be fixed.

239
00:20:15,835 --> 00:20:17,845
There is no need to worry.

240
00:20:38,765 --> 00:20:40,345
Alps!

241
00:20:45,515 --> 00:20:47,095
Prepare a strecther.

242
00:20:48,085 --> 00:20:49,665
Let's take our brothers.

243
00:20:50,185 --> 00:20:51,725
Yes, my Bey.

244
00:20:54,285 --> 00:20:55,605
The paintings.

245
00:20:58,525 --> 00:21:00,095
They are entrusted.

246
00:21:01,215 --> 00:21:02,735
We have to take them.

247
00:21:09,585 --> 00:21:11,335
We need them.

248
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,725
Aygül!

249
00:21:12,805 --> 00:21:14,055
Çoban!

250
00:21:14,105 --> 00:21:15,635
It's a trap!

251
00:21:28,195 --> 00:21:29,495
No! No!

252
00:21:29,565 --> 00:21:30,805
No! No!

253
00:21:30,805 --> 00:21:32,125
Aygül!

254
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:36,135
Aygül! Aygül! No! Aygül!
No!

255
00:21:36,215 --> 00:21:37,485
Aygül!

256
00:21:37,575 --> 00:21:39,435
Aygül look at me!

257
00:21:39,525 --> 00:21:41,095
Open your eyes!

258
00:21:41,135 --> 00:21:42,185
Aygül!
Open your eyes!

259
00:21:42,235 --> 00:21:43,545
Open your eyes!

260
00:21:49,885 --> 00:21:51,925
You are fine!

261
00:21:52,025 --> 00:21:53,355
Are you all right?

262
00:21:53,415 --> 00:21:54,755
I am fine.

263
00:21:54,845 --> 00:21:57,375
I am fine. I am fine.

264
00:22:03,605 --> 00:22:04,905
It is all right.

265
00:22:06,125 --> 00:22:07,465
It is all right now.

266
00:22:07,475 --> 00:22:08,635
Çoban!

267
00:22:08,725 --> 00:22:10,485
Çoban, Cerkutay!

268
00:22:10,485 --> 00:22:12,345
Çoban! Çoban!

269
00:22:12,425 --> 00:22:15,535
Get back! Get back! Çoban!

270
00:22:16,145 --> 00:22:18,725
Brother! Çoban!

271
00:22:18,775 --> 00:22:20,095
Çoban!

272
00:22:20,145 --> 00:22:24,455
Çoban! Çoban! Çoban!
My brother!

273
00:22:27,325 --> 00:22:30,485
We did this so that it would explode
in the chest of the infidel.

274
00:22:34,465 --> 00:22:36,485
This is fate.

275
00:22:37,575 --> 00:22:39,435
We were shot with our own.

276
00:22:40,355 --> 00:22:42,875
You are not going anywhere, brother!

277
00:22:43,125 --> 00:22:45,645
Where are you going before we fight
the infidel?

278
00:22:58,565 --> 00:23:00,885
That is what I am saying, brother
Cerkutay.

279
00:23:02,745 --> 00:23:05,945
The conquests will be done
without me but...

280
00:23:06,465 --> 00:23:07,965
...my heart is relieved.

281
00:23:08,765 --> 00:23:10,485
The conquests will be made.

282
00:23:20,685 --> 00:23:22,015
Brother...

283
00:23:22,725 --> 00:23:24,425
...tell me Bey, brother.

284
00:23:26,115 --> 00:23:27,975
Tell him to bless his right to me.

285
00:23:34,555 --> 00:23:35,915
Brother...

286
00:23:40,395 --> 00:23:42,645
...a Turk can't be prisoned...

287
00:23:45,055 --> 00:23:46,555
...before he dies.

288
00:23:49,695 --> 00:23:53,285
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah...

289
00:23:54,285 --> 00:24:00,945
...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant and Messenger of Allah.

290
00:24:01,405 --> 00:24:02,715
No!

291
00:24:02,885 --> 00:24:06,015
No! No! No! No! No!

292
00:24:06,085 --> 00:24:07,595
No!

293
00:24:08,225 --> 00:24:09,925
No!

294
00:24:11,045 --> 00:24:14,945
He is gone! He is gone Cerkutay!

295
00:24:15,415 --> 00:24:18,125
Come on, Çoban! Come on!

296
00:24:18,225 --> 00:24:21,425
Come on, Çoban! Come on!
Come on!

297
00:24:28,635 --> 00:24:30,705
Osman will be torn into pieces...

298
00:24:32,905 --> 00:24:34,915
...just like his alps.

299
00:24:35,215 --> 00:24:37,295
We are just starting, Barkın.

300
00:24:38,755 --> 00:24:40,305
Osman didn't die but...

301
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:44,685
...he will watch the destruction of his
reputation and loved ones.

302
00:24:44,945 --> 00:24:48,565
We took everyone he trusted with us
but...

303
00:24:48,915 --> 00:24:50,635
...Turgut and Kosses...

304
00:24:50,655 --> 00:24:52,655
...they still showed up.

305
00:24:53,015 --> 00:24:56,145
It means we're not attacking hard enough,
Barkın.

306
00:24:57,145 --> 00:25:00,485
You will not stop until their swords are
against each other.

307
00:25:00,805 --> 00:25:03,435
There will not be a single place
they have not been hit.

308
00:25:03,645 --> 00:25:05,165
Those who were asleep woke up.

309
00:25:05,985 --> 00:25:10,485
And burned them with the ammunition
they thought they would conquer.

310
00:25:25,005 --> 00:25:27,515
It will explode the moment someone
walks in.

311
00:25:31,765 --> 00:25:34,295
You are like a snake among them, Cornelia.

312
00:25:34,705 --> 00:25:37,445
No, I am just a poor loyal woman.

313
00:25:40,025 --> 00:25:42,375
They took Mari here as well.

314
00:25:43,865 --> 00:25:46,405
What you've learned from Mari will
be useful.

315
00:25:47,865 --> 00:25:50,945
Thanks to you, we will shoot Osman
with his own arm.

316
00:25:54,165 --> 00:25:56,685
But no one will ever suspect me.

317
00:25:57,665 --> 00:26:02,675
What harm could a woman mourning for her
lady do?

318
00:26:04,305 --> 00:26:07,355
You will be too harmful, Cornelia.

319
00:26:07,355 --> 00:26:08,735
Too harmful.

320
00:26:10,135 --> 00:26:11,515
Too harmful.

321
00:26:16,335 --> 00:26:18,035
While we explode Söğüt...

322
00:26:18,725 --> 00:26:20,765
...you will play a game to Gündüz.

323
00:26:21,935 --> 00:26:27,225
If you succeed, everyone will believe that
Gunduz burned Söğüt to escape.

324
00:26:37,635 --> 00:26:39,665
It will be so easy.

325
00:26:47,395 --> 00:26:52,055
I am not only destroying his people but
I am destroying everything.

326
00:26:52,905 --> 00:26:55,725
Cornelia must be finished now.

327
00:26:57,045 --> 00:26:59,605
Oh my dear Cornelia.

328
00:27:00,145 --> 00:27:02,655
There is nothing she can't do.

329
00:27:03,455 --> 00:27:07,515
What if Osman forgives Gündüz?

330
00:27:08,745 --> 00:27:13,615
Osman can't take all the pressure and
forgive Gündüz.

331
00:27:14,065 --> 00:27:15,395
He will kill him.

332
00:27:16,345 --> 00:27:19,625
Then we reveal the innocence of Gündüz
and...

333
00:27:19,905 --> 00:27:22,475
...burn Osman's heart.

334
00:27:23,225 --> 00:27:24,785
Will he kill him?

335
00:27:24,785 --> 00:27:26,565
If he doesn't...

336
00:27:26,655 --> 00:27:29,815
...neither Kosses nor Turgut won't forgive
him.

337
00:27:30,125 --> 00:27:32,715
In this case, they will kill Gündüz.

338
00:27:33,695 --> 00:27:35,065
Barkın...

339
00:27:35,175 --> 00:27:38,715
...those who don't attend the war win it.

340
00:27:38,965 --> 00:27:41,125
We are not the ones who are fighting...

341
00:27:41,205 --> 00:27:43,155
...but the ones who are starting the war.

342
00:27:43,545 --> 00:27:45,565
Darkness always wins.

343
00:27:59,285 --> 00:28:01,375
Give this poison to Cornelia.

344
00:28:01,835 --> 00:28:05,415
A poison that even the most skilled
healer cannot understand.

345
00:28:08,005 --> 00:28:09,595
Odorless.

346
00:28:10,115 --> 00:28:11,705
Invisible.

347
00:28:12,855 --> 00:28:17,585
We will hasten the fading of that
weak light of Oğuz.

348
00:28:23,355 --> 00:28:26,475
Söğüt will surrender to a dark fear.

349
00:29:09,295 --> 00:29:11,045
Who did this?

350
00:29:33,555 --> 00:29:35,875
We had enemies from inside.

351
00:29:37,385 --> 00:29:39,745
We beheaded all of them.

352
00:29:41,465 --> 00:29:43,965
We had enemies from outside.

353
00:29:45,445 --> 00:29:48,035
We crashed them with our swords.

354
00:29:50,365 --> 00:29:51,745
But...

355
00:29:53,865 --> 00:29:55,885
...but this...

356
00:29:56,975 --> 00:30:00,585
...is a devil hiding in the darkness!

357
00:30:13,245 --> 00:30:15,065
We will be on alert.

358
00:30:17,325 --> 00:30:19,045
That devil can hide.

359
00:30:20,905 --> 00:30:23,505
I will speak the language he understands.

360
00:30:43,525 --> 00:30:46,025
There is nowhere else to go, Gündüz Bey.

361
00:30:46,085 --> 00:30:47,785
We will return to the tribe.

362
00:30:48,565 --> 00:30:50,845
You can't escape justice!

363
00:30:50,845 --> 00:30:53,845
Selvi Hatun, we are running for justice!

364
00:30:54,285 --> 00:30:56,325
We are running to justify ourselves.

365
00:30:56,325 --> 00:30:59,185
Don't push it, Gündüz Bey!

366
00:31:02,105 --> 00:31:03,805
If that so...

367
00:31:04,025 --> 00:31:06,025
...you gave me no other choice.

368
00:31:06,765 --> 00:31:08,145
Hatun!

369
00:31:30,205 --> 00:31:32,745
Will you kill me too, Ayşe Hatun?

370
00:31:33,585 --> 00:31:35,165
Run, my Bey!

371
00:31:36,525 --> 00:31:38,045
Ayşe!

372
00:31:39,585 --> 00:31:40,885
Come on!

373
00:31:48,365 --> 00:31:51,395
Söğüt

374
00:31:51,725 --> 00:31:53,465
There is no trace.

375
00:31:53,765 --> 00:31:56,105
Alps searched everywhere.

376
00:31:56,525 --> 00:32:00,265
Whoever did the explosion is someone who
knows Söğüt well.

377
00:32:01,645 --> 00:32:03,645
I don't want to say it but...

378
00:32:04,905 --> 00:32:06,905
...it is someone among us.

379
00:32:09,345 --> 00:32:11,605
I don't know, Osman Bey.

380
00:32:12,465 --> 00:32:15,545
Once a traitor always a traitor.

381
00:32:16,045 --> 00:32:20,385
Tell me, does anyone know Söğüt better
than Gündüz?

382
00:32:22,565 --> 00:32:25,085
This is such a huge game that...

383
00:32:25,585 --> 00:32:27,665
...only the devil can pull it off.

384
00:32:30,265 --> 00:32:32,125
I don't know who the enemy is.

385
00:32:32,285 --> 00:32:35,785
But I know his cruelty well.

386
00:32:39,985 --> 00:32:42,025
My brother is not cruel.

387
00:32:43,445 --> 00:32:45,625
Of course, he made mistakes...

388
00:32:46,425 --> 00:32:47,765
...but...

389
00:32:48,605 --> 00:32:51,185
He would never do such a vile thing.

390
00:32:52,565 --> 00:32:55,305
He would never harm our people and home
like this.

391
00:32:55,985 --> 00:32:58,345
There is evidence, Osman Bey.

392
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:01,545
Who killed my family is Gündüz.

393
00:33:02,365 --> 00:33:04,365
Can we come in, my Bey?

394
00:33:04,925 --> 00:33:06,705
Come in!

395
00:33:07,905 --> 00:33:09,465
In the name of Allah.

396
00:33:21,085 --> 00:33:22,385
Tell me.

397
00:33:23,145 --> 00:33:24,465
My Bey...

398
00:33:27,605 --> 00:33:28,905
...Akça.

399
00:33:33,105 --> 00:33:34,825
What happened to Akça?

400
00:33:36,045 --> 00:33:37,425
It was a trap.

401
00:33:40,485 --> 00:33:43,365
They set a trap in the tent, my Bey.

402
00:33:45,345 --> 00:33:47,365
Akça Çoban...

403
00:33:47,905 --> 00:33:49,455
...is martyred.

404
00:33:49,645 --> 00:33:51,365
What are you saying?

405
00:33:55,885 --> 00:33:57,425
Akça!

406
00:34:02,645 --> 00:34:04,205
Başsungur.

407
00:34:04,985 --> 00:34:07,505
They killed the guardian alps too, my Bey.

408
00:34:10,364 --> 00:34:13,125
They destroyed everything on their way.

409
00:34:16,425 --> 00:34:18,465
They also burned the catapults.

410
00:34:21,145 --> 00:34:22,725
Akça!

411
00:34:22,985 --> 00:34:24,485
Akça!

412
00:34:37,860 --> 00:34:41,070
"Verily we belong to Allah and verily
to him do we return."

413
00:34:44,465 --> 00:34:46,605
This is such an enemy that...

414
00:34:49,364 --> 00:34:53,745
...he doesn't even have a shadow.

415
00:34:55,085 --> 00:34:57,625
He clearly hides in the dark.

416
00:34:58,985 --> 00:35:00,765
But I will find him.

417
00:35:01,925 --> 00:35:03,465
I will find him.

418
00:35:11,145 --> 00:35:13,245
Tell us as well, Osman Bey.

419
00:35:14,005 --> 00:35:15,685
How?

420
00:35:18,025 --> 00:35:20,805
I have a prisoner from those who attacked
the tavern.

421
00:35:21,985 --> 00:35:24,145
I'll make him talk and learn the truth.

422
00:35:27,945 --> 00:35:29,665
Can I come in, my Bey?

423
00:35:29,665 --> 00:35:30,985
Come in!

424
00:35:32,825 --> 00:35:34,585
In the name of Allah.

425
00:35:39,445 --> 00:35:40,985
Osman Bey...

426
00:35:42,285 --> 00:35:44,065
...the rascal tried to escape.

427
00:35:44,805 --> 00:35:46,305
He tried to kill me.

428
00:35:49,685 --> 00:35:51,425
I had to kill him.

429
00:35:54,685 --> 00:35:56,425
What are you saying?

430
00:35:57,085 --> 00:35:59,625
How do you do that without asking me?

431
00:36:00,245 --> 00:36:03,025
My Bey! My Bey!

432
00:36:03,025 --> 00:36:05,025
He tried to kill us.

433
00:36:05,965 --> 00:36:08,005
He injured Barkın Bey as well.

434
00:36:08,585 --> 00:36:11,805
We searched the whole Söğüt but couldn't
find anyone.

435
00:36:44,385 --> 00:36:48,835
I swear that I will burn these devils
alive who burned my heart...

436
00:36:49,025 --> 00:36:51,065
...to the ground!

437
00:36:51,445 --> 00:36:54,445
They should fear my rage!

438
00:37:07,105 --> 00:37:11,145
It is great that the Söğüt burned down,
Argus.

439
00:37:12,585 --> 00:37:15,945
Also they blame Gündüz for all of this.

440
00:37:16,185 --> 00:37:17,765
Good.

441
00:37:17,885 --> 00:37:19,425
Good.

442
00:37:21,185 --> 00:37:27,205
Both Kosses and Turgut can't trust Osman
anymore.

443
00:37:27,205 --> 00:37:29,205
What about Gündüz?

444
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:32,185
He is a dead man now.

445
00:37:32,185 --> 00:37:34,185
We can say that.

446
00:37:34,185 --> 00:37:36,725
What will we gain from all this, sir?

447
00:37:39,265 --> 00:37:44,325
Both Kosses and Turgut will grow apart
from Osman.

448
00:37:46,065 --> 00:37:49,825
Someone wants to leave Osman alone.

449
00:37:50,865 --> 00:37:52,585
But who?

450
00:37:53,445 --> 00:37:55,965
Who is this secret ally of us?

451
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:58,065
Who?

452
00:38:07,005 --> 00:38:09,585
Sir, I was told to convey this to you.

453
00:38:18,365 --> 00:38:19,925
You!

454
00:38:23,185 --> 00:38:25,685
Of course, you!

455
00:38:26,865 --> 00:38:31,545
No one could make such a great move
but you.

456
00:38:31,545 --> 00:38:33,545
Who could?

457
00:38:39,165 --> 00:38:40,745
All right.

458
00:38:42,445 --> 00:38:45,505
Father, come on.

459
00:38:45,505 --> 00:38:47,505
Open your eyes.

460
00:38:51,485 --> 00:38:53,005
Allah is the healer.

461
00:38:53,385 --> 00:38:54,945
Allah is the healer.

462
00:38:55,425 --> 00:38:56,965
Allah is the healer.

463
00:39:03,245 --> 00:39:05,765
Allah is the healer, Bala Hatun.

464
00:39:05,865 --> 00:39:07,865
Allah is the healer.

465
00:39:13,845 --> 00:39:18,405
Hang on, my Sheik, hang on!

466
00:39:39,405 --> 00:39:42,285
There is always hope, Bala Hatun.

467
00:39:42,485 --> 00:39:44,005
We will pray.

468
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:46,745
Thank you.

469
00:39:50,685 --> 00:39:52,225
Father!

470
00:39:54,565 --> 00:39:55,945
Allah...

471
00:39:56,745 --> 00:40:00,985
...may you give healing to my Sheik.

472
00:40:02,785 --> 00:40:04,025
Father!

473
00:40:04,045 --> 00:40:05,805
He is burning!

474
00:40:05,805 --> 00:40:07,865
Do something, Kumral Abdal!

475
00:40:07,865 --> 00:40:09,865
He is burning!

476
00:40:14,325 --> 00:40:16,405
I hope this will work.

477
00:40:18,325 --> 00:40:20,865
In the name of Allah.

478
00:40:22,645 --> 00:40:24,205
Allah is the healer.

479
00:40:26,225 --> 00:40:27,745
Allah is the healer.

480
00:40:31,405 --> 00:40:32,925
Allah is the healer.

481
00:40:33,125 --> 00:40:34,625
Allah is the healer.

482
00:40:37,485 --> 00:40:39,005
Allah is the healer.

483
00:40:39,465 --> 00:40:42,505
Allah is the healer.

484
00:40:44,625 --> 00:40:45,945
My Sheik.

485
00:40:47,145 --> 00:40:48,665
Akça Dervish...

486
00:40:49,665 --> 00:40:52,165
...the service must continue at the lodge.

487
00:40:52,705 --> 00:40:54,725
Thank you, İbrahim Fakih.

488
00:40:56,345 --> 00:40:59,925
Tell me whatever is missing in the lodge.

489
00:41:00,425 --> 00:41:04,645
It is a blessing to me to serve the
household where Allah is remembered...

490
00:41:04,645 --> 00:41:06,405
...and where Allah's friends are.

491
00:41:06,845 --> 00:41:08,403
Of course, we will.

492
00:41:08,775 --> 00:41:10,985
May Allah be pleased with you.

493
00:41:11,775 --> 00:41:15,795
There is not much needed to serve
the lodge.

494
00:41:42,475 --> 00:41:44,005
There isn't anyone.

495
00:41:46,485 --> 00:41:48,485
They lost our track.

496
00:41:50,485 --> 00:41:53,625
We are fighting our family.

497
00:41:54,355 --> 00:41:56,865
What do we do, Gündüz?

498
00:41:58,415 --> 00:42:01,475
We will get rid of the slanders, my Ayşe.

499
00:42:02,765 --> 00:42:04,505
Everything will be fine.

500
00:42:06,365 --> 00:42:08,405
We are innocent.

501
00:42:08,425 --> 00:42:10,505
The truth will come out.

502
00:42:12,155 --> 00:42:13,685
Eventually.

503
00:42:17,345 --> 00:42:20,625
What if we die like this?

504
00:42:22,005 --> 00:42:23,525
Then...

505
00:42:26,875 --> 00:42:29,905
...what will happen to our son?

506
00:42:31,415 --> 00:42:34,015
I wish I could see my son one more time.

507
00:42:37,695 --> 00:42:39,725
I wish I could, Gündüz.

508
00:42:47,645 --> 00:42:49,215
My Ayşe.

509
00:42:51,515 --> 00:42:54,815
Allah is not with those who give up...

510
00:42:55,165 --> 00:42:57,445
...he is with those who are patient.

511
00:42:58,735 --> 00:43:00,715
We will be patient.

512
00:43:03,695 --> 00:43:05,935
We will be patient.

513
00:43:15,075 --> 00:43:16,595
Erdoğdu?

514
00:43:19,005 --> 00:43:20,245
Erdoğdu?

515
00:43:21,115 --> 00:43:24,465
Ayşe! Ayşe! Ayşe!

516
00:44:00,225 --> 00:44:02,695
This is the end, Gündüz Bey!

517
00:44:32,365 --> 00:44:33,895
Amen.

518
00:45:03,345 --> 00:45:04,925
Bala...

519
00:45:12,535 --> 00:45:14,065
My Bala!

520
00:45:18,765 --> 00:45:20,285
My Bala.

521
00:45:22,445 --> 00:45:23,955
My Bala.

522
00:45:25,495 --> 00:45:27,995
The good and evil is from Allah.

523
00:45:28,285 --> 00:45:30,395
We will bear it.

524
00:45:31,125 --> 00:45:32,885
We know that...

525
00:45:33,805 --> 00:45:36,675
...none of us is eternal in this world.

526
00:45:37,695 --> 00:45:39,885
It hurts so bad, my Osman!

527
00:45:40,135 --> 00:45:41,265
So bad!

528
00:45:41,305 --> 00:45:43,365
Everything is for us, my Bala.

529
00:45:43,395 --> 00:45:45,135
Everything is for us.

530
00:45:45,515 --> 00:45:47,655
Don't lose hope.

531
00:45:48,655 --> 00:45:50,245
But...

532
00:45:59,555 --> 00:46:01,855
...we must be prepared for anything.

533
00:46:04,915 --> 00:46:07,945
Allah is the one who gives and takes.

534
00:46:08,135 --> 00:46:10,145
We will heal.

535
00:46:10,215 --> 00:46:11,735
We will be patient.

536
00:46:12,645 --> 00:46:15,005
We will be strong.

537
00:46:17,085 --> 00:46:19,135
You are a strong Hatun.

538
00:46:19,385 --> 00:46:20,915
You will get through this.

539
00:46:21,495 --> 00:46:23,015
You will be patient.

540
00:46:37,345 --> 00:46:39,945
Söğüt is filled with snakes, Kosses.

541
00:46:40,755 --> 00:46:43,085
They don't leave a trace.

542
00:46:43,275 --> 00:46:45,435
You can't feel their breath.

543
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:48,855
But it poisons everywhere.

544
00:46:49,685 --> 00:46:54,725
Everything happened after the Vizier died
and Geyhatu left.

545
00:46:56,125 --> 00:46:59,155
Do you think the Sultan is involved in
this?

546
00:46:59,585 --> 00:47:02,105
Would he get involved in such a thing...

547
00:47:02,805 --> 00:47:06,885
...to damage Osman's power? If that
is the case...

548
00:47:06,975 --> 00:47:10,015
...Gündüz is the best pawn for this job.

549
00:47:10,645 --> 00:47:12,715
I don't think it is the Sultan.

550
00:47:13,085 --> 00:47:15,155
This is a new devil.

551
00:47:15,525 --> 00:47:18,105
That Gündüz will be justified for sure.

552
00:47:18,305 --> 00:47:21,555
He was just about to be put on a trial
but these happened.

553
00:47:21,845 --> 00:47:24,885
He worked with that traitor Vezir before
as well.

554
00:47:25,015 --> 00:47:28,535
It seems Gündüz Bey got skillful
in this area.

555
00:47:28,585 --> 00:47:31,665
Right.

556
00:47:42,025 --> 00:47:44,525
You are slouching Samuel.

557
00:47:44,895 --> 00:47:47,465
This is bad news.

558
00:47:48,635 --> 00:47:50,655
Gündüz Bey ran away.

559
00:47:50,955 --> 00:47:53,555
What do you mean he ran away?

560
00:47:57,855 --> 00:48:00,425
Ah, Osman Bey, ah!

561
00:48:00,805 --> 00:48:04,595
This is what happens when you don't do
justice in time.

562
00:48:04,865 --> 00:48:10,025
Gündüz burnt the tavern and killed many
innocent people. He won't stop after all.

563
00:48:10,895 --> 00:48:12,645
I've waited Kosses.

564
00:48:12,845 --> 00:48:15,225
I've waited so he gets fairly judged.

565
00:48:15,495 --> 00:48:18,005
I've waited so he gets the appropriate
sentence.

566
00:48:18,115 --> 00:48:20,385
But he chose to escape.

567
00:48:20,935 --> 00:48:22,985
Oh, Gündüz.

568
00:48:23,415 --> 00:48:25,115
Now that you ran away...

569
00:48:25,155 --> 00:48:28,965
...you will be killed by me even if you go
to hell.

570
00:48:30,075 --> 00:48:32,375
Don't worry, we will find him.

571
00:48:32,615 --> 00:48:34,755
Send news to everywhere, Samuel.

572
00:48:34,975 --> 00:48:39,165
I will drown the one who brings him to me
alive or dead in gold.

573
00:48:40,005 --> 00:48:42,925
-Now, go!
-Yes, Sir.

574
00:48:45,655 --> 00:48:47,735
Ah, Osman Bey!

575
00:48:48,445 --> 00:48:49,805
Ah!

576
00:49:11,955 --> 00:49:13,465
Alps!

577
00:49:16,305 --> 00:49:18,825
We buried our martyrs.

578
00:49:19,855 --> 00:49:21,745
Those dogs attacked us...

579
00:49:21,965 --> 00:49:25,125
...in a way that suits them.

580
00:49:25,805 --> 00:49:31,185
Their intention is to bow our heads.

581
00:49:33,055 --> 00:49:35,105
But...

582
00:49:35,485 --> 00:49:38,195
...we won't let them enjoy.

583
00:49:39,925 --> 00:49:44,575
Those who face us don't live long.

584
00:49:45,195 --> 00:49:48,015
They hide their daggers.

585
00:49:48,855 --> 00:49:51,355
They attack from the shadows.

586
00:49:53,965 --> 00:50:00,965
We will lighten them up out of the
darkness they are in with our faith.

587
00:50:01,125 --> 00:50:09,635
We'll bring their end with
the sword of justice!

588
00:50:09,655 --> 00:50:12,765
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

589
00:50:13,035 --> 00:50:24,855
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

590
00:50:29,375 --> 00:50:30,945
Come on.

591
00:50:32,265 --> 00:50:34,545
Osman Bey.

592
00:50:39,545 --> 00:50:42,815
Your heart is even bigger than what
I've heard, Osman Bey.

593
00:50:43,875 --> 00:50:46,905
Your faith is even stronger than
what I've heard.

594
00:50:47,525 --> 00:50:54,425
I've learned from my father Ertuğrul Ghazi
and Sheik Edebali.

595
00:50:54,665 --> 00:50:55,995
Thank you.

596
00:50:56,585 --> 00:50:58,345
But...

597
00:50:59,485 --> 00:51:03,025
whenever I face a difficult conflict...

598
00:51:03,895 --> 00:51:06,425
I always went to Sheik Edebali.

599
00:51:06,655 --> 00:51:09,175
But now he is in death's bed.

600
00:51:10,785 --> 00:51:13,365
Death comes from Allah, Osman Bey.

601
00:51:13,535 --> 00:51:16,085
Edebali is the light of the Oghuzs.

602
00:51:16,175 --> 00:51:19,045
You've been enlightened by
him all this time.

603
00:51:20,505 --> 00:51:22,585
You will find a way out.

604
00:51:23,185 --> 00:51:25,295
Söğüt on one side..

605
00:51:25,615 --> 00:51:28,375
Kayı on the other...

606
00:51:29,565 --> 00:51:32,945
They want to involve my brother
into this.

607
00:51:33,835 --> 00:51:37,005
When Söğüt is struggling
with death...

608
00:51:37,275 --> 00:51:40,295
now my brother is a part
of the problem.

609
00:51:41,085 --> 00:51:43,255
This creates a greater problem.

610
00:51:44,145 --> 00:51:46,225
It'll be solved eventually, but...

611
00:51:49,505 --> 00:51:53,185
What does Allah say in the verse?

612
00:51:53,255 --> 00:51:54,375
''O' believers!

613
00:51:54,405 --> 00:51:58,905
Keep justice for Allah.

614
00:51:59,455 --> 00:52:09,000
Be people who testify for justice.
Don't let your grudges take you astray.

615
00:52:09,575 --> 00:52:14,345
Be just. This is most appropriate.

616
00:52:15,635 --> 00:52:17,735
Be afraid of Allah.

617
00:52:18,115 --> 00:52:22,835
Without a doubt, Allah knows
what you do.''

618
00:52:26,125 --> 00:52:29,945
I heard that, your brother,
Gündüz Bey...

619
00:52:30,505 --> 00:52:34,885
made such mistakes before too.

620
00:52:36,915 --> 00:52:39,885
And you forgave him, Osman Bey.

621
00:52:42,195 --> 00:52:47,405
The evidence is clear. An innocent's
blood shouldn't be on you.

622
00:52:48,415 --> 00:52:53,465
You are the bey.
You should make your decision soon.

623
00:52:54,455 --> 00:52:55,965
It's your verdict.

624
00:52:58,755 --> 00:53:03,615
If the justice is late, it's not just.

625
00:53:04,875 --> 00:53:07,405
Justice will be served.

626
00:53:20,115 --> 00:53:22,645
Many innocent people faded away
in Söğüt.

627
00:53:22,895 --> 00:53:25,325
Why is Osman Bey facing this?

628
00:53:25,905 --> 00:53:27,455
You are right.

629
00:53:27,615 --> 00:53:32,335
Your brother kills the wife of
your commander. What is this?

630
00:53:33,225 --> 00:53:34,725
Beys.

631
00:53:37,685 --> 00:53:41,005
The rest is gossip.

632
00:53:42,135 --> 00:53:44,135
Don't eat a Muslim's flesh.

633
00:53:44,445 --> 00:53:46,985
Not every finger on a hand
is the same.

634
00:53:47,635 --> 00:53:51,635
It's apparent. Gündüz Bey is
not like Osman Bey.

635
00:53:53,865 --> 00:53:57,695
Osman Bey carries the sword of
justice.

636
00:53:58,635 --> 00:54:02,225
He'll kill Gündüz and his wife.

637
00:54:03,015 --> 00:54:06,525
We say the same.
He will, surely.

638
00:54:07,895 --> 00:54:09,455
But...

639
00:54:10,025 --> 00:54:14,335
let's say we are wrong,
Osman Bey can't rule justly...

640
00:54:15,405 --> 00:54:16,935
then...

641
00:54:17,385 --> 00:54:22,435
as the Kızılbeyoğlu beys,
we'll take our position.

642
00:54:25,025 --> 00:54:29,095
He works with lords, rebels.
He can't protect anyone.

643
00:54:30,365 --> 00:54:34,945
I don't believe that he can secure
the justice. He cdo it sooner.

644
00:54:35,795 --> 00:54:39,955
This way or another.
Everything will be revealed.

645
00:54:40,625 --> 00:54:43,355
Nothing will be left in the dark.

646
00:54:46,655 --> 00:54:48,005
Son.

647
00:54:48,285 --> 00:54:52,355
We did it, mother.
We buried our martyrs.

648
00:54:53,895 --> 00:54:55,675
Now...

649
00:55:11,035 --> 00:55:13,815
Traitor!

650
00:55:38,025 --> 00:55:40,805
Traitors!

651
00:56:00,185 --> 00:56:03,125
Traitors!

652
00:56:05,755 --> 00:56:08,755
Traitors!

653
00:56:12,225 --> 00:56:16,035
With Erdoğdu's help, they escaped
in barrels, Osman Bey.

654
00:56:16,405 --> 00:56:19,465
We caught them in the
cave before too late.

655
00:56:22,125 --> 00:56:24,155
Traitors!

656
00:56:28,305 --> 00:56:31,135
Boran. Cerkutay.
Bring him.

657
00:56:31,345 --> 00:56:32,885
My bey.

658
00:57:36,675 --> 00:57:38,545
Why did you run, brother?

659
00:57:41,265 --> 00:57:44,805
Why did you run, brother?

660
00:57:53,065 --> 00:57:54,605
Why?

661
00:58:13,065 --> 00:58:15,635
Take my brother to the caged tent.

662
00:58:15,675 --> 00:58:17,385
As you order, my bey.

663
00:58:33,155 --> 00:58:37,675
Traitor!

664
00:58:54,325 --> 00:58:57,415
Traitor!

665
00:58:59,255 --> 00:59:01,265
Thank you.

666
00:59:02,915 --> 00:59:05,915
You saved Gündüz Bey from
a great mistake.

667
00:59:28,485 --> 00:59:33,575
My Allah. Protect my children
and the unity of the tribe.

668
00:59:40,635 --> 00:59:43,365
You've done a great job, Cornelia.

669
00:59:43,705 --> 00:59:46,225
Will you say something, Barkın Bey?

670
00:59:46,725 --> 00:59:49,275
I don't have much time.

671
00:59:55,025 --> 00:59:56,845
For Selcan.

672
01:00:01,475 --> 01:00:04,845
Don't worry. Her time will come too.

673
01:00:05,635 --> 01:00:08,725
But this is for the never-ending
light of the Oghuz.

674
01:00:09,925 --> 01:00:14,955
Kumral Abdal creates medicines
to heal Edebali.

675
01:00:15,625 --> 01:00:17,685
We must stop it.

676
01:00:18,725 --> 01:00:21,315
Edebali shouldn't wake up, Cornelia.

677
01:00:29,755 --> 01:00:33,195
I'll kill that light with my own hands.

678
01:00:50,905 --> 01:00:52,415
Osman.

679
01:01:19,435 --> 01:01:21,005
Osman Bey.

680
01:01:21,085 --> 01:01:23,085
We didn't do anything.

681
01:01:59,015 --> 01:02:02,025
My brother wouldn't kill
an innocent baby.

682
01:02:04,645 --> 01:02:06,165
Why did you run away?

683
01:02:06,355 --> 01:02:10,915
I heard it. They attacked Söğüt.
They see me responsible for that too?

684
01:02:11,335 --> 01:02:13,055
Why did you run?

685
01:02:13,075 --> 01:02:14,885
Don't you trust my justice?

686
01:02:14,885 --> 01:02:18,055
Not at all. They want to put
everything on me, Osman!

687
01:02:18,645 --> 01:02:20,985
Did I have any other choice
to clean my name?

688
01:02:20,985 --> 01:02:23,825
They want to put in on us, not you.

689
01:02:23,875 --> 01:02:25,475
They want to break us.

690
01:02:25,825 --> 01:02:28,915
Don't you know that running away
makes you guilty?

691
01:02:29,595 --> 01:02:31,105
Why didn't you think?

692
01:02:31,365 --> 01:02:34,845
I didn't feel like dying before finding
who did all this, brother.

693
01:02:37,445 --> 01:02:39,325
I'll find that traitor.

694
01:02:40,715 --> 01:02:43,855
You believe me. Dying is not a
problem now.

695
01:02:44,055 --> 01:02:45,755
You will die, brother.

696
01:02:49,085 --> 01:02:52,155
I didn't believe you.
I'm searching for the truth.

697
01:02:56,615 --> 01:03:00,645
And the truth will be revealed
when you die.

698
01:03:22,615 --> 01:03:25,375
Those who serve an ancient goal...

699
01:03:28,455 --> 01:03:32,495
are like a tree that's roots go
to the center of the world.

700
01:03:32,655 --> 01:03:36,745
And time is a horrific storm.

701
01:03:38,065 --> 01:03:47,155
It bends that tree but it can't
take it off.

702
01:03:52,035 --> 01:03:53,405
You didn't forget it.

703
01:03:53,575 --> 01:03:55,615
That's why I'm alive.

704
01:03:59,565 --> 01:04:01,125
Master Darius.

705
01:04:01,705 --> 01:04:03,585
I can't believe my eyes.

706
01:04:03,635 --> 01:04:06,175
Time didn't even touch you.

707
01:04:06,765 --> 01:04:11,595
Nikola. Nikola. My naughtiest student.

708
01:04:16,265 --> 01:04:18,005
Still apple?

709
01:04:18,285 --> 01:04:20,305
It symbolizes Adam's sin.

710
01:04:20,605 --> 01:04:22,845
And reminds me of my sins.

711
01:04:24,305 --> 01:04:28,305
Master Darius, forgive my curiosity.

712
01:04:30,605 --> 01:04:32,165
Why now?

713
01:04:33,005 --> 01:04:38,465
While I was fighting this difficult
war with stupid treacherous...

714
01:04:38,465 --> 01:04:42,475
lords and a fool emperor...

715
01:04:43,365 --> 01:04:47,545
while these barbarians were invading
our lands, why was I alone?

716
01:04:47,545 --> 01:04:48,935
Why now?

717
01:04:49,965 --> 01:04:54,845
I didn't think you would struggle this
much to destroy a little Turkish bey.

718
01:04:58,185 --> 01:05:00,275
You disappointed me.

719
01:05:00,915 --> 01:05:04,055
But don't worry.
I'm here now.

720
01:05:06,205 --> 01:05:09,485
In Osman's heart.

721
01:05:15,855 --> 01:05:21,645
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun.

722
01:05:25,405 --> 01:05:31,515
are accused of Turgut Bey's wife,
Michael Kosses' sister...

723
01:05:34,775 --> 01:05:38,795
and our guest...

724
01:05:40,965 --> 01:05:43,535
Mari's murder.

725
01:05:47,585 --> 01:05:51,125
I was forgiven when I went astray
from the right path.

726
01:05:52,885 --> 01:05:55,385
Now, I'm being trialed with a slander.

727
01:05:55,455 --> 01:05:57,975
I don't even have a single
word to say.

728
01:05:59,815 --> 01:06:03,315
My bey, we did nothing.

729
01:06:06,665 --> 01:06:09,215
Why are you still letting
them talk, Osman Bey?

730
01:06:10,095 --> 01:06:12,865
Why are you letting them
pierce my heart further?

731
01:06:13,515 --> 01:06:15,095
Turgut Bey.

732
01:06:22,545 --> 01:06:25,605
Boran. Bring the evidence.

733
01:06:46,555 --> 01:06:50,555
Say it. Did this bowl come
out of your tent.

734
01:06:53,465 --> 01:06:55,355
It belongs to us, my bey.

735
01:07:01,105 --> 01:07:02,985
And you...

736
01:07:03,605 --> 01:07:08,455
can you swear that you took this
bowl from Ayşe Hatun, Cornelia?

737
01:07:10,445 --> 01:07:18,295
I wish my hands were broken so that
I couldn't take it.

738
01:07:20,775 --> 01:07:23,605
Ayşe Hatun gave it to me with
her own hands.

739
01:07:26,745 --> 01:07:28,825
I took it.

740
01:07:30,225 --> 01:07:34,235
The flask that poisoned my sister
was in their tent.

741
01:07:34,665 --> 01:07:37,175
What are you still questioning,
Osman Bey?

742
01:07:37,345 --> 01:07:39,125
The truth, Kosses.

743
01:07:40,925 --> 01:07:42,305
The truth.

744
01:07:44,845 --> 01:07:47,225
She kidnapped my wife
with the vizier first.

745
01:07:48,225 --> 01:07:51,295
Now, he killed her for who knows
whom, Osman Bey!

746
01:07:51,375 --> 01:07:52,875
This is the truth.

747
01:07:52,875 --> 01:07:55,225
You keep saying the same thing, Turgut!

748
01:07:55,225 --> 01:07:56,545
Gündüz!

749
01:07:57,125 --> 01:07:58,645
And you, Kosses?

750
01:08:01,185 --> 01:08:02,945
Who did I give Mari to?

751
01:08:03,455 --> 01:08:08,235
I gave Mari to you, for the security
of my tribe.

752
01:08:09,195 --> 01:08:11,245
It's you who gave her to Nikola.

753
01:08:14,735 --> 01:08:17,274
Shut up, Gündüz Bey.

754
01:08:17,415 --> 01:08:20,665
Don't try to cover your guilt
with my faults.

755
01:08:23,274 --> 01:08:25,755
You will die today.

756
01:08:26,125 --> 01:08:28,694
Only I can decide that, Kosses!

757
01:08:30,965 --> 01:08:32,465
Be decent.

758
01:08:36,885 --> 01:08:38,965
When your turn comes...

759
01:08:40,135 --> 01:08:41,725
you will speak.

760
01:08:55,335 --> 01:08:57,165
-Saltuk.
-My bey.

761
01:09:03,925 --> 01:09:05,295
Come on.

762
01:09:25,035 --> 01:09:30,564
With a slander, you took Gündüz
apart from Osman.

763
01:09:30,925 --> 01:09:32,465
Genious!

764
01:09:34,035 --> 01:09:37,175
Kosses, Turgut, they will fall apart.

765
01:09:37,705 --> 01:09:39,765
What else does he have?

766
01:09:40,984 --> 01:09:44,524
We got what he has.

767
01:09:44,825 --> 01:09:47,005
But he has outer support, Nikola.

768
01:09:47,005 --> 01:09:49,095
I heard that Umur died.

769
01:09:49,095 --> 01:09:52,875
Osman buried Umur with his own hands.

770
01:09:53,595 --> 01:09:56,905
Ivaz is next.
I'll kill him.

771
01:09:58,435 --> 01:10:00,725
Osman will take caution.

772
01:10:01,575 --> 01:10:03,725
He won't make the same mistake.

773
01:10:04,895 --> 01:10:07,055
While you kill him...

774
01:10:07,155 --> 01:10:10,235
I'll take Kosses to my side.

775
01:10:10,235 --> 01:10:12,285
No. No.

776
01:10:12,285 --> 01:10:14,385
Osman might be after something.

777
01:10:14,965 --> 01:10:16,735
We'll be careful.

778
01:10:17,265 --> 01:10:22,015
You won't contact until you are sure
that Kosses and Turgut aren't with him.

779
01:10:23,155 --> 01:10:24,745
So, master...

780
01:10:27,555 --> 01:10:29,555
what do you want from me?

781
01:10:32,975 --> 01:10:36,835
You were unseated.
You were insulted.

782
01:10:37,945 --> 01:10:43,215
Did your grudge take it's
direction to Turgut Bey who replaced you?

783
01:10:43,965 --> 01:10:46,675
We aren't nailed to these seats,
Osman Bey.

784
01:10:47,305 --> 01:10:49,825
We paid the price of our mistake.

785
01:10:50,705 --> 01:10:53,885
I have no grudge nor greed.

786
01:10:57,255 --> 01:10:59,035
Especially against a woman.

787
01:11:03,465 --> 01:11:05,705
Especially against a woman who
carries a child.

788
01:11:05,765 --> 01:11:10,615
Don't speak my sister's name!

789
01:11:11,535 --> 01:11:13,255
Whatever the verdict is...

790
01:11:13,255 --> 01:11:14,965
I will kill you, Gündüz!

791
01:11:14,965 --> 01:11:16,555
Kosses!

792
01:11:18,525 --> 01:11:20,555
Let me go!

793
01:11:28,115 --> 01:11:29,585
It's your sister!

794
01:11:32,095 --> 01:11:33,875
But she died in my tribe.

795
01:11:35,755 --> 01:11:37,885
And it's my brother who is
accused.

796
01:11:40,085 --> 01:11:43,855
The verdict is mine to give.

797
01:11:46,385 --> 01:11:51,275
Either sit or leave!

798
01:12:03,495 --> 01:12:05,305
I'm silent for now...

799
01:12:06,925 --> 01:12:08,485
Osman Bey.

800
01:12:11,125 --> 01:12:13,785
If your verdict isn't just...

801
01:12:18,975 --> 01:12:24,135
then, I'll serve the justice
with my sword.

802
01:12:25,595 --> 01:12:28,155
If you don't get convinced
of my justice...

803
01:12:30,845 --> 01:12:33,105
you can use your sword.

804
01:12:35,975 --> 01:12:37,535
But know that...

805
01:12:39,975 --> 01:12:41,985
I won't hold back.

806
01:12:48,145 --> 01:12:49,685
Alright.

807
01:13:16,675 --> 01:13:18,265
Gündüz Bey.

808
01:13:20,215 --> 01:13:25,445
You giving Mari out earlier,
shows an example.

809
01:13:28,415 --> 01:13:32,915
Your anger against Turgut Bey and Kosses,
shows a reason.

810
01:13:35,685 --> 01:13:41,955
The poison being found in your tent,
shows evidence.

811
01:13:46,915 --> 01:13:48,665
And running away...

812
01:13:51,105 --> 01:13:53,275
is accepting your crime.

813
01:14:02,555 --> 01:14:04,115
Gündüz Bey.

814
01:14:04,975 --> 01:14:07,235
If it's a slander, you will speak.

815
01:14:08,475 --> 01:14:10,505
You can't bow down to slander.

816
01:14:15,155 --> 01:14:16,695
Speak now.

817
01:14:22,045 --> 01:14:25,125
Come, my girl.
Come, sit.

818
01:14:26,095 --> 01:14:28,595
-Did you do what I said?
-Yes, Mother Selcan.

819
01:14:29,225 --> 01:14:32,045
May it heal our sheik.

820
01:14:33,175 --> 01:14:35,345
Go and bring a bowl.
I'll prepare the herbs.

821
01:14:35,345 --> 01:14:36,695
Alright.

822
01:14:49,965 --> 01:14:52,525
Is this for Sheik Edebali, Mother Selcan?

823
01:14:52,945 --> 01:14:55,535
Yes, my girl.
I boiled bone broth.

824
01:14:55,535 --> 01:14:57,325
After adding the herbs...

825
01:14:57,325 --> 01:15:00,825
our sheik will be on his feet soon.

826
01:15:23,645 --> 01:15:26,755
I'll do it, Zehra.
Help Mother Selcan.

827
01:15:31,705 --> 01:15:33,975
A little more.

828
01:15:43,865 --> 01:15:45,715
Like this.

829
01:15:47,215 --> 01:15:49,745
Is it good now?

830
01:15:55,675 --> 01:15:57,755
Bring it, my girl.

831
01:16:04,095 --> 01:16:05,845
Bring it here.

832
01:16:07,955 --> 01:16:10,455
Take it there before
it gets cold.

833
01:16:10,875 --> 01:16:13,405
I should go. Maybe they'll
need help.

834
01:16:13,925 --> 01:16:15,195
Go, my girl.

835
01:16:27,065 --> 01:16:29,265
I stepped back from my mistake,
Osman Bey.

836
01:16:31,115 --> 01:16:34,375
A Muslim can't be bit from the
same spot twice.

837
01:16:38,325 --> 01:16:39,895
And about this matter...

838
01:16:41,235 --> 01:16:44,945
I'm not involved with anything.

839
01:16:47,275 --> 01:16:52,575
But it seems that the one who set
the trap thought of everything.

840
01:17:02,775 --> 01:17:05,655
Has anyone seen Gündüz Bey with
poison on his hand?

841
01:17:15,735 --> 01:17:21,575
Has anyone seen Ayşe Hatun putting
poison to the food?

842
01:17:33,295 --> 01:17:35,835
But they were seen
running away from the tribe.

843
01:17:37,655 --> 01:17:39,745
If I hadn't caught them...

844
01:17:40,375 --> 01:17:45,465
Gündüz Bey would be with his
allies now.

845
01:17:47,075 --> 01:17:49,285
Why would an innocent man run,
Osman Bey?

846
01:17:53,905 --> 01:17:56,745
Have you ever been slandered?

847
01:17:58,465 --> 01:17:59,845
Tell me.

848
01:18:02,485 --> 01:18:05,055
May Allah give it to no one.

849
01:18:07,835 --> 01:18:10,415
The one who wants to clean his
name would run.

850
01:18:11,705 --> 01:18:14,875
The one who doesn't want to die with
a stain would run.

851
01:18:19,805 --> 01:18:22,855
The one who doesn't trust the justice
of his brother...

852
01:18:25,325 --> 01:18:26,625
would run.

853
01:18:30,665 --> 01:18:35,165
Forgive me, my bey. But it was me
who led him to escape.

854
01:18:35,495 --> 01:18:38,575
If there is a fault, it's mine.

855
01:18:53,415 --> 01:18:59,435
There are evidence to prove
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun are guilty.

856
01:19:04,675 --> 01:19:06,715
But no one has seen it.

857
01:19:11,785 --> 01:19:13,525
It's the bey's verdict.

858
01:19:19,285 --> 01:19:24,335
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun will
be banished.

859
01:19:26,715 --> 01:19:28,255
Osman Bey.

860
01:19:28,995 --> 01:19:31,495
This isn't right, Osman Bey.

861
01:19:31,975 --> 01:19:33,775
This isn't.

862
01:19:33,855 --> 01:19:36,895
Your tribe has no justice!

863
01:19:41,165 --> 01:19:43,185
Shame on you.

864
01:19:44,405 --> 01:19:46,445
Shame on you.

865
01:19:59,095 --> 01:20:04,625
People! Osman Bey banished
Gündüz Bey.

866
01:20:14,125 --> 01:20:16,655
Do you hear it, Osman?

867
01:20:17,625 --> 01:20:19,685
You hear it.

868
01:20:21,485 --> 01:20:23,265
Lord Kosses.

869
01:20:25,705 --> 01:20:27,535
Don't act with fury.

870
01:20:28,005 --> 01:20:31,395
This isn't right.
This isn't right.

871
01:20:31,575 --> 01:20:33,645
Osman wasn't just.

872
01:20:33,886 --> 01:20:35,277
It's not easy.

873
01:20:35,355 --> 01:20:36,915
It's his brother.

874
01:20:36,935 --> 01:20:38,955
Osman Bey can't kill Gündüz Bey.

875
01:20:39,015 --> 01:20:40,115
He made...

876
01:20:40,115 --> 01:20:41,655
many mistakes...

877
01:20:41,655 --> 01:20:43,235
but he forgave him.

878
01:20:43,235 --> 01:20:45,235
I knew this would happen.

879
01:20:45,355 --> 01:20:47,735
And the dead is my sister.

880
01:20:47,915 --> 01:20:49,995
With a baby on her belly.

881
01:20:50,675 --> 01:20:54,715
Osman owes me two lives, not one.

882
01:20:54,715 --> 01:20:58,235
You are right, Kosses.
It's great pain.

883
01:20:58,335 --> 01:21:00,335
You are right to do anything.

884
01:21:08,335 --> 01:21:10,335
I swear, Mari.

885
01:21:11,195 --> 01:21:14,035
I'll take our revenge.

886
01:21:15,615 --> 01:21:17,615
I swear.

887
01:21:18,895 --> 01:21:21,175
Giros. Samuel.
We are leaving.

888
01:21:23,515 --> 01:21:25,035
Osman.

889
01:21:25,835 --> 01:21:30,575
This destroyed the people's trust
for you.

890
01:21:31,455 --> 01:21:33,475
You hanged yourself.

891
01:21:36,155 --> 01:21:37,655
Come on.

892
01:21:37,655 --> 01:21:39,655
We want justice!

893
01:21:40,745 --> 01:21:42,815
Söğüt

894
01:21:49,055 --> 01:21:51,555
What is it, sisters?
Why are you here?

895
01:21:51,575 --> 01:21:53,715
Mother Selcan prepared soup for my sheik.

896
01:21:53,715 --> 01:21:55,275
We brought it.

897
01:22:02,135 --> 01:22:03,675
May it heal my sheik.

898
01:22:03,675 --> 01:22:05,215
Thank you, sisters.

899
01:22:05,215 --> 01:22:06,555
Proceed.

900
01:22:06,575 --> 01:22:08,615
No need to make it
crowded in here.

901
01:22:08,675 --> 01:22:10,435
One person is enough.

902
01:22:11,815 --> 01:22:13,515
We aren't of the same faith.

903
01:22:13,555 --> 01:22:15,555
But let me get his prayers.

904
01:22:21,595 --> 01:22:22,895
Go on.

905
01:22:28,935 --> 01:22:31,695
God damn you!

906
01:22:31,695 --> 01:22:39,175
Traitors!

907
01:22:43,895 --> 01:22:47,895
Answer for your crimes!

908
01:22:47,895 --> 01:22:52,415
We want justice!

909
01:22:53,455 --> 01:22:56,795
We want justice!

910
01:22:56,935 --> 01:22:58,435
Traitors!

911
01:23:12,355 --> 01:23:22,715
We want justice!

912
01:23:24,175 --> 01:23:25,755
We want justice!

913
01:23:28,775 --> 01:23:30,295
Traitors!

914
01:23:30,955 --> 01:23:32,655
We want justice!

915
01:23:34,715 --> 01:23:36,235
We want justice!

916
01:23:46,235 --> 01:23:48,315
It can't go unpunished.

917
01:23:48,515 --> 01:23:50,315
-Boran.
-My bey.

918
01:23:50,795 --> 01:23:53,315
Alps should get Gündüz Bey
on the road.

919
01:23:53,775 --> 01:23:56,275
They'll company him until
a safe place.

920
01:23:56,295 --> 01:23:57,875
As you order, my bey.

921
01:23:57,875 --> 01:23:59,755
Traitors!

922
01:23:59,755 --> 01:24:01,575
We want justice!

923
01:24:01,575 --> 01:24:03,375
Justice!

924
01:24:03,375 --> 01:24:08,255
Answer for your crime!

925
01:24:18,355 --> 01:24:23,955
We want justice!

926
01:24:24,935 --> 01:24:30,415
We want justice!

927
01:24:54,135 --> 01:24:55,695
Alps.

928
01:24:55,995 --> 01:24:57,695
Return to the tribe.

929
01:24:58,375 --> 01:25:00,455
We'll settle in a inn and rest.

930
01:25:02,555 --> 01:25:05,555
Valiants. The tribe is under
your protection.

931
01:25:13,455 --> 01:25:14,815
Come on.

932
01:25:24,075 --> 01:25:26,135
What will we do, Gündüz?

933
01:25:26,195 --> 01:25:28,255
Where will we go?

934
01:25:33,395 --> 01:25:34,955
Wait.

935
01:25:43,815 --> 01:25:45,895
What is it, Gündüz Bey?

936
01:25:46,415 --> 01:25:50,575
Where are you going this
freely?

937
01:25:56,455 --> 01:25:57,815
Kosses.

938
01:25:57,835 --> 01:25:59,395
Let Ayşe go.

939
01:25:59,415 --> 01:26:01,115
Settle it with me.

940
01:26:01,655 --> 01:26:03,175
No.

941
01:26:05,035 --> 01:26:07,055
You didn't settle it with me.

942
01:26:08,395 --> 01:26:11,115
Your wife poisoned my
sister with her own hands.

943
01:26:11,755 --> 01:26:15,835
My sister and the baby
in her belly.

944
01:26:19,095 --> 01:26:22,175
You owe me two lives, Gündüz Bey.

945
01:26:22,275 --> 01:26:25,575
Neither she nor I did
nothing to anyone!

946
01:26:26,935 --> 01:26:28,975
But if you'll feel relieved...

947
01:26:29,515 --> 01:26:32,035
come at me.
I won't die without fighting.

948
01:26:32,135 --> 01:26:33,475
Ayşe.

949
01:26:33,475 --> 01:26:35,015
Protect yourself.

950
01:26:35,015 --> 01:26:36,285
Look for an opportunity.

951
01:26:36,285 --> 01:26:37,395
Come on.

952
01:26:39,595 --> 01:26:41,155
Come, Kosses.

953
01:26:41,155 --> 01:26:42,535
I will.

954
01:26:43,335 --> 01:26:44,635
I will.

955
01:26:53,975 --> 01:26:55,275
Gündüz!

956
01:27:01,815 --> 01:27:03,135
Insolent!

957
01:27:20,075 --> 01:27:21,595
Ayşe...

958
01:27:24,595 --> 01:27:26,755
Make your last prayer, Gündüz Bey.

959
01:27:30,055 --> 01:27:31,795
For my sister.

960
01:27:36,435 --> 01:27:39,675
Gündüz!

961
01:27:47,035 --> 01:27:49,075
With the name of Allah.

962
01:27:55,295 --> 01:27:57,635
Soup will help him, right?

963
01:27:58,815 --> 01:28:00,895
Inshallah, Bala Hatun.

964
01:28:00,975 --> 01:28:02,515
Inshallah.

965
01:28:02,915 --> 01:28:04,975
I can smell it.

966
01:28:05,675 --> 01:28:09,755
Mother Selcan must've put healing
ingredients.

967
01:28:11,115 --> 01:28:15,875
It will heal my sheik, inshallah.

968
01:28:18,335 --> 01:28:19,895
Inshallah.

969
01:28:21,915 --> 01:28:23,955
Allah is healing.

970
01:28:24,335 --> 01:28:26,415
We ask for your help.

971
01:28:46,815 --> 01:28:48,835
May it be good, my Allah.

972
01:28:52,155 --> 01:28:54,175
With the name of Allah.

973
01:28:55,855 --> 01:28:58,435
May it be good, Bala Hatun.

974
01:29:00,315 --> 01:29:01,895
I should take it away.

975
01:29:44,995 --> 01:29:48,575
With the name of Allah.

976
01:30:01,775 --> 01:30:03,355
Allah is healing.

977
01:30:35,135 --> 01:30:37,015
Now is time for duty.

978
01:30:38,175 --> 01:30:39,955
What is it, Osman Bey?

979
01:30:39,975 --> 01:30:43,035
Go to the lord of İğnehisar.

980
01:30:44,415 --> 01:30:46,675
Scare him for good.

981
01:30:48,555 --> 01:30:50,575
He is oppressing people.

982
01:30:50,975 --> 01:30:53,485
He is creating problems
for Turkish merchants.

983
01:30:54,255 --> 01:30:55,775
Tell him that...

984
01:30:56,775 --> 01:30:59,335
if he wants to live
peacefully in his castle...

985
01:31:00,495 --> 01:31:02,515
he'll give the taxes in time.

986
01:31:04,475 --> 01:31:05,995
What if he doesn't?

987
01:31:08,155 --> 01:31:10,735
It will be a conquest, my bey?

988
01:31:11,615 --> 01:31:13,695
They don't expect that for now.

989
01:31:15,435 --> 01:31:19,835
But we'll act when they think
we sleep.

990
01:31:22,035 --> 01:31:26,655
When they expect the least,
we'll ruin their world.

991
01:31:28,555 --> 01:31:30,595
İğnehisar is an important castle.

992
01:31:31,295 --> 01:31:32,875
If we take it...

993
01:31:34,215 --> 01:31:36,775
the gates of İnegöl will be opened.

994
01:31:37,055 --> 01:31:38,575
Great.

995
01:31:38,875 --> 01:31:40,975
Nawruz is here and the conquests
start.

996
01:31:43,815 --> 01:31:45,835
It's time for the Muslims to smile.

997
01:31:56,455 --> 01:31:58,695
May Allah heal our sheik.

998
01:32:00,535 --> 01:32:02,875
Get him on his foot in no time.

999
01:32:04,835 --> 01:32:06,375
Malhun.

1000
01:32:06,755 --> 01:32:09,955
Could Gündüz Bey get in Edebali's
blood too?

1001
01:32:12,515 --> 01:32:14,575
I'm talking about the explosion
in Söğüt.

1002
01:32:15,515 --> 01:32:17,255
No, Selvi.

1003
01:32:17,375 --> 01:32:19,155
I don't believe that.

1004
01:32:19,795 --> 01:32:21,795
What's there to not believe?

1005
01:32:21,795 --> 01:32:24,335
They escaped the tribe at
the time of the explosion.

1006
01:32:24,355 --> 01:32:26,795
They drew weapons against me.

1007
01:32:27,675 --> 01:32:29,735
Everything is obvious.

1008
01:32:30,335 --> 01:32:32,715
Whoever Gündüz Bey is working
with...

1009
01:32:32,795 --> 01:32:35,315
they want to kill Osman Bey.

1010
01:32:38,515 --> 01:32:40,555
Is it something they haven't done before?

1011
01:32:41,935 --> 01:32:43,995
Haven't you told me?

1012
01:32:45,095 --> 01:32:47,975
I don't know, Selvi.
I don't know.

1013
01:32:50,295 --> 01:32:52,175
Since my father became a martyr...

1014
01:32:52,855 --> 01:32:54,915
I'm all mixed up.

1015
01:32:55,155 --> 01:32:57,195
Gündüz Bey is two-faced.

1016
01:32:58,215 --> 01:33:00,235
He played well.

1017
01:33:00,995 --> 01:33:03,075
He worked with the Mongols.

1018
01:33:04,115 --> 01:33:06,635
Didn't Mongols kill my uncle?

1019
01:33:06,995 --> 01:33:08,995
The one who works with the Mongols...

1020
01:33:09,075 --> 01:33:10,815
can do anything, sister.

1021
01:33:10,895 --> 01:33:13,475
Do you think all this
happens for nothing?

1022
01:33:14,495 --> 01:33:16,375
Mari, Söğüt...

1023
01:33:16,755 --> 01:33:18,075
my uncle.

1024
01:33:19,875 --> 01:33:21,875
Where does all this point at?

1025
01:33:22,855 --> 01:33:24,915
What are you saying, Selvi?

1026
01:33:24,995 --> 01:33:27,575
Would Gündüz Bey go this far?

1027
01:33:29,715 --> 01:33:32,215
Do you say he killed my
father too?

1028
01:34:04,095 --> 01:34:08,135
When he gives out his money,
he thinks justice is served.

1029
01:34:10,935 --> 01:34:13,435
Is this your justice?

1030
01:34:45,095 --> 01:34:46,675
My bey.

1031
01:34:47,055 --> 01:34:48,635
Our scouts.

1032
01:34:52,155 --> 01:34:54,715
They found Gündüz Bey's headgear
on the road.

1033
01:34:55,755 --> 01:35:00,275
It seems that they were attacked.

1034
01:35:02,555 --> 01:35:05,595
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun.

1035
01:35:09,735 --> 01:35:11,255
They were killed.

1036
01:35:11,255 --> 01:35:12,755
No!

1037
01:35:13,695 --> 01:35:16,715
My children!

1038
01:35:17,375 --> 01:35:18,735
What...

1039
01:35:45,235 --> 01:35:48,535
They are gone!

1040
01:35:58,835 --> 01:36:01,985
May Allah forgive their sins,
Mother Selcan.

1041
01:36:07,275 --> 01:36:08,795
Osman.

1042
01:36:14,055 --> 01:36:17,615
Osman, why did you send
your brother away?

1043
01:36:17,715 --> 01:36:21,975
What did you do, Osman?

1044
01:36:45,135 --> 01:36:50,715
Whoever makes a decision
over mine...

1045
01:36:51,895 --> 01:36:53,415
will pay the price.

1046
01:36:54,075 --> 01:36:56,215
Whoever has done it
did well.

1047
01:37:00,355 --> 01:37:02,935
The one who took Gündüz's head...

1048
01:37:02,935 --> 01:37:04,975
have made the decision
you couldn't make.

1049
01:37:07,795 --> 01:37:10,315
The justice is served now, Osman Bey.

1050
01:37:10,515 --> 01:37:12,015
Turgut Bey.

1051
01:37:12,495 --> 01:37:14,075
Osman Bey!

1052
01:37:17,075 --> 01:37:18,655
Know your place!

1053
01:37:19,695 --> 01:37:21,735
I know my place!

1054
01:37:22,495 --> 01:37:24,515
You should've known justice.

1055
01:37:24,595 --> 01:37:26,175
But no.

1056
01:37:26,175 --> 01:37:28,995
You are an enemy to the
one who serves justice.

1057
01:37:29,195 --> 01:37:31,275
Tell me it's a lie, Osman Bey.

1058
01:37:31,355 --> 01:37:33,895
I stood with you and lost my alps.

1059
01:37:34,375 --> 01:37:35,935
I walked on your path...

1060
01:37:36,035 --> 01:37:38,075
and lost my wife, child.

1061
01:37:38,075 --> 01:37:40,195
Do you know what I have left?

1062
01:37:43,355 --> 01:37:44,875
The blood of my loved ones.

1063
01:37:46,215 --> 01:37:47,775
Now, take no offense.

1064
01:37:48,795 --> 01:37:50,875
My deal is done.

1065
01:37:50,955 --> 01:37:53,775
You don't know your words
because of your anger.

1066
01:37:54,215 --> 01:37:56,075
Calm your anger first.

1067
01:37:56,335 --> 01:37:58,155
Then, we'll have a talk.

1068
01:37:58,735 --> 01:38:00,315
Now, leave!

1069
01:38:01,315 --> 01:38:04,015
Alps! We are returning
to our tribe.

1070
01:38:04,985 --> 01:38:08,285
Our job here is done.

1071
01:38:13,785 --> 01:38:15,155
Come on!

1072
01:38:23,555 --> 01:38:25,135
Osman Bey.

1073
01:38:25,635 --> 01:38:28,385
Let them leave.
Blood can be refreshen.

1074
01:38:33,155 --> 01:38:35,705
Me and the Kızılbeyoğulları
are under your command.

1075
01:38:37,285 --> 01:38:40,035
We took the road with
people without hearts.

1076
01:38:49,835 --> 01:38:51,835
Thank you, Barkın.

1077
01:38:52,455 --> 01:38:54,035
Thank you.

1078
01:38:54,035 --> 01:38:58,285
Our hearts and arms are of steel.
We are with you.

1079
01:39:21,505 --> 01:39:24,185
Did our woods start to burn, Cornelia?

1080
01:39:28,385 --> 01:39:31,055
They did indeed, sir.

1081
01:39:32,355 --> 01:39:37,455
Kosses and Turgut so firmly
against Osman for releasing Gündüz.

1082
01:39:38,655 --> 01:39:42,385
Their unity is shaken to its core.

1083
01:39:45,455 --> 01:39:47,035
Good.

1084
01:39:48,835 --> 01:39:53,685
Now, it's time to throw bigger
woods on the fire.

1085
01:39:54,535 --> 01:39:56,535
What's our next goal, sir?

1086
01:39:57,185 --> 01:40:01,255
İhvaz is giving alps to Osman
with many.

1087
01:40:01,655 --> 01:40:03,355
He gives him weapons.

1088
01:40:04,285 --> 01:40:06,435
We must stop him.

1089
01:40:06,985 --> 01:40:08,755
We must get ahead of him.

1090
01:40:09,635 --> 01:40:11,755
Osman shouldn't get stronger.

1091
01:40:12,135 --> 01:40:13,905
He shouldn't get hopeful.

1092
01:40:14,355 --> 01:40:16,935
He shouldn't dream of Kızıl Elma.

1093
01:40:20,205 --> 01:40:22,055
Kızıl Elma!

1094
01:40:29,085 --> 01:40:30,655
Turks...

1095
01:40:31,305 --> 01:40:34,885
become dangerous when they dream.

1096
01:40:36,235 --> 01:40:38,985
I won't leave these lands
to the Muslims.

1097
01:40:39,535 --> 01:40:42,055
We'll kick them out
of these lands.

1098
01:40:42,055 --> 01:40:45,055
We'll take our holy lands back.

1099
01:40:47,905 --> 01:40:52,135
These lands will wet with their blood.

1100
01:40:53,085 --> 01:40:57,635
I'll bury them alive and
drown them in their blood.

1101
01:41:08,335 --> 01:41:09,835
They are gone.

1102
01:41:10,605 --> 01:41:11,935
They are gone.

1103
01:41:12,385 --> 01:41:14,885
Look at Ertuğrul Bey's son.

1104
01:41:15,655 --> 01:41:18,235
His grave is in a mountain.

1105
01:41:19,505 --> 01:41:21,085
He's gone...

1106
01:41:22,785 --> 01:41:25,355
Everyone is where they belong, sister.

1107
01:41:25,705 --> 01:41:28,255
Kosses did the right thing.

1108
01:41:30,355 --> 01:41:33,385
Is this how you depart, Gündüz?

1109
01:41:34,485 --> 01:41:37,535
Is this how I farewell you?

1110
01:41:40,305 --> 01:41:42,005
It's enough, mother.

1111
01:41:42,155 --> 01:41:44,385
Who are you weeping for?

1112
01:41:44,805 --> 01:41:47,085
They took many lives with them.

1113
01:41:47,655 --> 01:41:52,935
Enough, Malhun. My mother is sad.
Stop it!

1114
01:41:58,235 --> 01:41:59,755
Mother.

1115
01:42:00,655 --> 01:42:04,755
Bala, my girl. He is gone.
My Gündüz is gone.

1116
01:42:04,755 --> 01:42:06,755
My Ayşe is gone.

1117
01:42:12,205 --> 01:42:14,235
I don't want the bad for you, mother.

1118
01:42:14,655 --> 01:42:17,235
It's bad for the tears
you drop.

1119
01:42:21,185 --> 01:42:23,685
I know, he wouldn't.

1120
01:42:24,355 --> 01:42:26,705
Gündüz wouldn't do this.

1121
01:42:27,235 --> 01:42:29,955
They killed my children for nothing.

1122
01:42:29,955 --> 01:42:32,485
I'm burning inside.

1123
01:42:34,755 --> 01:42:38,335
Malhun Hatun, my mother is right.

1124
01:42:38,755 --> 01:42:41,335
I didn't believe any of it.

1125
01:42:41,655 --> 01:42:44,655
We are talking about Gündüz Bey
and Ayşe.

1126
01:42:44,685 --> 01:42:47,005
After all the things
he has done to us?

1127
01:42:48,035 --> 01:42:51,135
It was Gündüz Bey who gave
his neck to Osman Bey.

1128
01:42:51,685 --> 01:42:54,255
You don't know what to say
because of your pain.

1129
01:42:55,355 --> 01:42:57,885
Don't you see my mother?

1130
01:43:09,855 --> 01:43:12,855
Bala, tell me.

1131
01:43:12,855 --> 01:43:17,385
Is my sheik alright?
Please say yes.

1132
01:43:18,705 --> 01:43:21,285
Kumral Abdal is with him, mother.

1133
01:43:25,505 --> 01:43:27,035
Alps.

1134
01:43:27,935 --> 01:43:32,455
Shepherd Akça was preparing
ammunition for the war.

1135
01:43:33,855 --> 01:43:35,405
They killed him.

1136
01:43:36,535 --> 01:43:39,105
Sheik Edebali was illuminating
our way.

1137
01:43:39,605 --> 01:43:41,105
They attacked him.

1138
01:43:43,205 --> 01:43:45,705
They killed many of our alps.

1139
01:43:47,255 --> 01:43:49,535
Umur Bey was coming to aid us.

1140
01:43:50,205 --> 01:43:52,005
They killed him too.

1141
01:43:55,135 --> 01:43:57,155
Now it's İhvaz Bey.

1142
01:43:58,635 --> 01:44:01,355
They'll attack him as they
attacked Umur Bey.

1143
01:44:02,205 --> 01:44:04,205
But we'll get on the road...

1144
01:44:05,235 --> 01:44:07,085
and take İhvaz Bey.

1145
01:44:10,955 --> 01:44:12,985
-Boran.
-My bey.

1146
01:44:12,985 --> 01:44:14,335
-Baysungur.
-My bey.

1147
01:44:14,535 --> 01:44:16,635
Ready the fastest horses.

1148
01:44:16,985 --> 01:44:19,135
Fill your quivers with arrows.

1149
01:44:19,435 --> 01:44:21,935
-As you order, my bey.
-As you order, my bey.

1150
01:44:25,205 --> 01:44:26,555
Barkın.

1151
01:44:27,655 --> 01:44:29,655
Come with us.

1152
01:44:31,055 --> 01:44:33,305
İhvaz Bey will be happy
to see you.

1153
01:44:36,255 --> 01:44:38,305
I couldn't protect my uncle.

1154
01:44:38,905 --> 01:44:40,985
I want to protect my father-in-law.

1155
01:44:42,105 --> 01:44:45,185
Osman Bey. Gündüz Bey's death
shakened us too.

1156
01:44:45,855 --> 01:44:47,635
I want you to know.

1157
01:44:48,185 --> 01:44:51,555
You lost a brother.
But you gained one.

1158
01:45:25,055 --> 01:45:28,085
Stop, Kosses.
Stop.

1159
01:45:31,255 --> 01:45:35,335
What are you doing, Turgut?
First, you took my sister from me.

1160
01:45:35,635 --> 01:45:39,025
You couldn't protect her.
Are you here to protect her killer?

1161
01:45:39,235 --> 01:45:41,785
I'm not here to protect anyone, Kosses.

1162
01:45:43,455 --> 01:45:45,505
I came only with Konur.

1163
01:45:47,105 --> 01:45:48,605
To talk with you.

1164
01:45:50,935 --> 01:45:52,305
Speak.

1165
01:45:52,385 --> 01:45:54,455
Sheathe your sword first, Kosses.

1166
01:45:54,785 --> 01:45:56,805
Speak, Turgut.

1167
01:45:59,055 --> 01:46:01,155
Osman Bey says that it's a trap.

1168
01:46:02,185 --> 01:46:03,735
I believe him for now.

1169
01:46:05,005 --> 01:46:06,305
For now.

1170
01:46:06,305 --> 01:46:08,005
Tell me, Turgut.

1171
01:46:08,035 --> 01:46:12,355
What did Osman Bey tell you that
it convinced you?

1172
01:46:14,355 --> 01:46:15,885
Kosses.

1173
01:46:16,455 --> 01:46:18,185
Neither the vizier nor Geyhatu...

1174
01:46:18,505 --> 01:46:20,935
I've seen many treacherous
plots with my eyes...

1175
01:46:21,135 --> 01:46:23,135
whoever planned this plot.

1176
01:46:23,555 --> 01:46:25,605
Their aim is to leave Osman Bey alone.

1177
01:46:25,605 --> 01:46:28,885
Did they kill my Mari to isolate
Osman Bey?

1178
01:46:29,235 --> 01:46:30,985
Think, Kosses.

1179
01:46:31,685 --> 01:46:34,205
Gündüz and I are Osman's allies.

1180
01:46:35,355 --> 01:46:40,435
We are his comrades. The commanders
of his armies.

1181
01:46:44,205 --> 01:46:46,985
And you are his most precious ally.

1182
01:46:47,455 --> 01:46:51,635
Don't you see it? They destroyed us all
with a single move.

1183
01:46:53,455 --> 01:46:55,455
If Osman knew these...

1184
01:46:55,935 --> 01:46:59,005
he should've known that I would
attack Gündüz here.

1185
01:46:59,205 --> 01:47:02,935
He knew it. He banished Gündüz
knowingly.

1186
01:47:05,485 --> 01:47:07,255
Because now...

1187
01:47:09,055 --> 01:47:11,105
Gündüz has to die.

1188
01:47:12,485 --> 01:47:15,485
I can die, Turgut.
I can die.

1189
01:47:16,555 --> 01:47:19,085
I can do anything for Kayı.

1190
01:47:19,605 --> 01:47:23,605
So, who is attacking us, Turgut?

1191
01:47:23,655 --> 01:47:24,955
Who?

1192
01:47:24,955 --> 01:47:28,005
It must be someone in the darkness.

1193
01:47:29,535 --> 01:47:32,535
We have only one chance
to lure them to light.

1194
01:47:34,435 --> 01:47:37,785
You and I will be Osman's enemies.

1195
01:47:39,435 --> 01:47:42,435
And Gündüz must be dead.

1196
01:47:47,035 --> 01:47:48,785
For now, they'll think so.

1197
01:47:49,305 --> 01:47:52,305
Tell me, Turgut.

1198
01:47:53,105 --> 01:47:54,885
Why should I trust it?

1199
01:47:56,785 --> 01:47:59,355
Why should I spare Gündüz's life?

1200
01:48:00,885 --> 01:48:02,435
Don't.

1201
01:48:03,405 --> 01:48:07,155
Osman Bey wants you to keep
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun in your castle.

1202
01:48:10,185 --> 01:48:11,685
I want that...

1203
01:48:12,735 --> 01:48:15,255
if the evidence shows Gündüz's
direction...

1204
01:48:16,335 --> 01:48:18,855
you will execute him.

1205
01:48:23,705 --> 01:48:25,205
Both of them.

1206
01:48:27,885 --> 01:48:29,435
Alright.

1207
01:48:31,005 --> 01:48:33,055
You are alive for now.

1208
01:48:35,485 --> 01:48:36,985
For now.

1209
01:48:39,285 --> 01:48:42,855
Giros. Samuel. Take them.

1210
01:48:56,305 --> 01:48:58,835
It's time to expand the
plot at the tribe now.

1211
01:48:59,085 --> 01:49:01,605
You have the biggest mission.

1212
01:49:02,185 --> 01:49:06,035
We'll get out of these troubles
with new conquests.

1213
01:49:07,855 --> 01:49:10,485
-Stay in peace, Turgut Bey.
-Thank you.

1214
01:49:10,485 --> 01:49:12,235
May Allah bless your jihad.

1215
01:49:32,705 --> 01:49:34,205
From Barkın Bey.

1216
01:49:37,985 --> 01:49:42,305
My bey, it's from Kayı Tribe.
Barkın Bey sent it.

1217
01:49:55,135 --> 01:50:00,645
My brother, Umur Bey. He was killed
on his way to the Kayı Tribe.

1218
01:50:02,335 --> 01:50:04,905
If my father has fallen on this way...

1219
01:50:04,975 --> 01:50:08,565
we are on the right path.

1220
01:50:10,155 --> 01:50:12,375
Things are complicated at the tribe too.

1221
01:50:12,545 --> 01:50:14,845
It's not good.

1222
01:50:15,065 --> 01:50:17,325
They are filled with slackness.

1223
01:50:17,535 --> 01:50:19,745
Look at the borders, Serhat!

1224
01:50:19,815 --> 01:50:23,525
As soon as we came, we smelled
the battle.

1225
01:50:24,775 --> 01:50:26,595
My father is a martyr.

1226
01:50:26,865 --> 01:50:28,945
Inshallah, we'll be too.

1227
01:50:28,945 --> 01:50:30,525
Amin, my bey.

1228
01:50:31,135 --> 01:50:33,505
The caravan will continue on Kızılhan
road.

1229
01:50:33,755 --> 01:50:36,335
We'll go to Badirbük to
see Barkın.

1230
01:50:36,785 --> 01:50:38,855
Let's hear it form him.

1231
01:50:38,855 --> 01:50:43,395
My bey, do you know the messenger?
Maybe it's a trap?

1232
01:50:45,555 --> 01:50:48,615
If it's a trap, we'll kill
some heathens before reaching Kayı.

1233
01:50:49,205 --> 01:50:51,705
We'll tell them that we fought
on our way.

1234
01:50:52,885 --> 01:50:55,945
Come on!

1235
01:51:05,165 --> 01:51:09,235
The poison flows in Edebali's
veins.

1236
01:51:09,755 --> 01:51:11,895
My beautiful Cornelia.

1237
01:51:12,565 --> 01:51:16,385
Oghuz's weak light is fading
away forever.

1238
01:51:16,965 --> 01:51:18,985
The rest is darkness.

1239
01:51:19,405 --> 01:51:21,455
The darkness is ours, sir.

1240
01:51:24,675 --> 01:51:29,475
But, if you forgive my curiosity,
I want to ask something.

1241
01:51:29,655 --> 01:51:32,175
You can't learn without
asking, Cornelia.

1242
01:51:32,175 --> 01:51:34,175
My beautiful child.
Ask away.

1243
01:51:34,535 --> 01:51:37,595
This Turk, Barkın.

1244
01:51:38,635 --> 01:51:41,135
Why is he always with you?

1245
01:51:41,145 --> 01:51:45,645
We have nothing in commong. Even our
faiths are different.

1246
01:51:46,605 --> 01:51:49,155
Power-hunger, Cornelia.

1247
01:51:50,165 --> 01:51:54,705
Power-hunger makes you the dog
of your enemy.

1248
01:51:54,765 --> 01:51:56,845
We hold his leash.

1249
01:51:59,915 --> 01:52:02,115
I'll greet İhvaz now.

1250
01:52:02,115 --> 01:52:04,615
He must've received my letter.

1251
01:52:15,255 --> 01:52:18,495
No. You don't deserve this, sister.

1252
01:52:19,425 --> 01:52:21,465
You are right.

1253
01:52:22,435 --> 01:52:24,995
Gündüz Bey blinded them.

1254
01:52:26,915 --> 01:52:29,495
I can't understand it either.

1255
01:52:29,675 --> 01:52:32,215
Gündüz Bey is Osman's brother.

1256
01:52:32,215 --> 01:52:35,805
But you see it, Selvi.
Isn't it obvious.

1257
01:52:37,875 --> 01:52:39,965
You are right, sister.

1258
01:52:40,345 --> 01:52:41,865
But know it...

1259
01:52:42,285 --> 01:52:45,325
Bala Hatun tries to win Selcan Hatun's
favor.

1260
01:52:47,375 --> 01:52:50,875
No. Bala Hatun doesn't do
such things.

1261
01:52:56,485 --> 01:52:58,025
My dear sister.

1262
01:52:58,915 --> 01:53:01,225
You think everyone is like you.

1263
01:53:02,765 --> 01:53:04,775
But it isn't like that.

1264
01:53:05,385 --> 01:53:08,885
When it's about power...

1265
01:53:09,605 --> 01:53:11,645
no one knows anyone.

1266
01:53:13,365 --> 01:53:17,155
Brothers and sisters fight each other.

1267
01:53:25,095 --> 01:53:27,595
But you think that I'm being
sceptical.

1268
01:53:29,285 --> 01:53:32,355
Your beautiful heart knows the best.

1269
01:53:42,225 --> 01:53:44,755
Harmankaya Castle

1270
01:53:45,675 --> 01:53:49,715
Osman loves you so much, Gündüz Bey.

1271
01:53:55,355 --> 01:53:59,925
I never should've let my sister
join you.

1272
01:54:03,225 --> 01:54:13,385
I never should I let her leave
her safe castle to go to your tents.

1273
01:54:17,005 --> 01:54:19,085
Even if it's not by your hands...

1274
01:54:20,285 --> 01:54:22,375
she died because of you.

1275
01:54:23,025 --> 01:54:24,575
Spit, Kosses.

1276
01:54:25,255 --> 01:54:29,325
Spit your hatred through the slander.

1277
01:54:29,605 --> 01:54:30,955
Hatred?

1278
01:54:32,265 --> 01:54:34,345
Don't, Gündüz Bey.

1279
01:54:34,745 --> 01:54:36,985
If my sister hadn't die...

1280
01:54:38,425 --> 01:54:41,445
I almost loved you.

1281
01:54:49,745 --> 01:54:52,305
Sir, Lord Nikola is here.

1282
01:54:54,565 --> 01:54:56,565
You are already dead.

1283
01:54:56,615 --> 01:54:58,935
Don't let me hear anything.

1284
01:55:00,335 --> 01:55:02,655
Meanwhile, we'll see...

1285
01:55:03,645 --> 01:55:08,215
if Nikola is involved or not.

1286
01:55:21,335 --> 01:55:22,915
Sit.

1287
01:55:26,495 --> 01:55:28,585
Are you any better?

1288
01:55:37,420 --> 01:55:38,960
Kosses.

1289
01:55:40,650 --> 01:55:43,230
Did you really kill Kosses?

1290
01:55:50,630 --> 01:55:53,710
You didn't really ask me this
question, Nikola.

1291
01:55:54,550 --> 01:55:56,310
What was I supposed to do?

1292
01:55:56,330 --> 01:55:59,720
Let the murderer of my sister
live?

1293
01:56:00,960 --> 01:56:04,740
And Osman? What will he say
about this.

1294
01:56:06,740 --> 01:56:08,530
What will he say?

1295
01:56:09,410 --> 01:56:11,670
We both lost our siblings.

1296
01:56:11,960 --> 01:56:13,670
What can he say?

1297
01:56:14,390 --> 01:56:18,890
It's over. You are still friends
with Osman, then?

1298
01:56:19,110 --> 01:56:20,890
Don't be ridiculous, Nikola.

1299
01:56:21,520 --> 01:56:25,020
What friendship? Do you think
such a thing is still possible?

1300
01:56:26,430 --> 01:56:28,940
Osman was about to march my castle.

1301
01:56:29,480 --> 01:56:32,830
He lost his friends.
He lost his brother.

1302
01:56:33,460 --> 01:56:38,550
All his moves was in vain.

1303
01:56:39,460 --> 01:56:42,170
Osman lost everything.

1304
01:56:47,880 --> 01:56:51,900
So, our castles are safe.

1305
01:56:52,500 --> 01:56:54,000
They are.

1306
01:57:29,890 --> 01:57:31,460
Salam Alaikum.

1307
01:57:44,180 --> 01:57:49,890
There is no God but Allah.
He is one. He owns everything.

1308
01:57:50,290 --> 01:57:54,560
And Muhammad is the messenger
of Allah.

1309
01:58:01,140 --> 01:58:02,720
Alaikum Salam.

1310
01:58:04,020 --> 01:58:06,040
You are obviously on the Allah's path.

1311
01:58:06,980 --> 01:58:12,030
Where are you coming from, old man?
Where are you going to?

1312
01:58:13,160 --> 01:58:18,250
I'm coming from Söğüt to
wherever our path leads to.

1313
01:58:19,120 --> 01:58:20,650
Söğüt, then.

1314
01:58:21,860 --> 01:58:24,230
I'm on my way to Kayı Tribe.

1315
01:58:25,080 --> 01:58:26,450
I know it.

1316
01:58:29,880 --> 01:58:32,760
All the beys are coming to the borders.

1317
01:58:33,090 --> 01:58:36,670
Osman Bey has been struggling for the
unity of the Turks.

1318
01:58:42,260 --> 01:58:45,890
True. The hope of the Turks
lie on the borders.

1319
01:58:46,740 --> 01:58:51,800
When we are united, neither the Byzantines
nor the Mongols can stop us.

1320
01:58:55,860 --> 01:59:01,940
The Muslim unity starts by
performing the salaat together.

1321
01:59:01,940 --> 01:59:03,520
Let's come together.

1322
01:59:03,620 --> 01:59:07,210
But let the bey be our imam.

1323
01:59:08,770 --> 01:59:10,100
Thank you.

1324
01:59:59,110 --> 02:00:02,430
My bey. The cart went
this way.

1325
02:00:02,740 --> 02:00:06,050
But ten horsemen went
this way.

1326
02:00:12,660 --> 02:00:13,970
The ones who departed...

1327
02:00:14,370 --> 02:00:17,410
are either İhvaz Bey or
the scouts.

1328
02:00:22,060 --> 02:00:24,650
But this isn't going to the Kayı Tribe.

1329
02:00:36,760 --> 02:00:39,350
They went to Kayı Tribe from here.

1330
02:00:40,250 --> 02:00:43,770
But these tracks...

1331
02:00:48,340 --> 02:00:51,450
it seems that they separated
İhvaz Bey from the caravan.

1332
02:00:52,780 --> 02:00:56,460
Cerkutay, Boran, Barkın.

1333
02:00:56,710 --> 02:00:58,230
Come with us.

1334
02:00:58,230 --> 02:01:00,290
The others will follow
the caravan.

1335
02:01:00,290 --> 02:01:03,220
As you order, my bey.

1336
02:01:07,370 --> 02:01:09,910
You shouldn't find the master, Osman.

1337
02:01:09,970 --> 02:01:11,710
I can't allow this.

1338
02:01:29,550 --> 02:01:31,070
Allahu Akbar.

1339
02:01:45,750 --> 02:01:47,290
Allahu Akbar.

1340
02:01:50,130 --> 02:01:52,200
Allah listens to those who praise him.

1341
02:01:54,300 --> 02:01:55,820
Allahu Akbar.

1342
02:01:59,660 --> 02:02:01,160
Allahu Akbar.

1343
02:02:03,500 --> 02:02:05,000
Allahu Akbar.

1344
02:02:10,030 --> 02:02:11,570
Allahu Akbar!

1345
02:02:42,610 --> 02:02:45,110
What will you do with Osman?

1346
02:02:46,880 --> 02:02:48,460
He is already done.

1347
02:02:48,460 --> 02:02:50,180
His beys turned their backs
on him.

1348
02:02:50,420 --> 02:02:53,300
Why are you still going to him?

1349
02:02:54,140 --> 02:02:56,170
Peace and mercy of Allah be on you.

1350
02:02:56,350 --> 02:02:58,940
Umur wanted to reach Osman too.

1351
02:03:00,020 --> 02:03:02,020
It wasn't his destiny.

1352
02:03:02,820 --> 02:03:05,120
Peace and mercy of Allah be on you.

1353
02:03:36,580 --> 02:03:41,800
The borders have many valiants.

1354
02:03:42,600 --> 02:03:46,450
But they have many traitors too.

1355
02:03:47,780 --> 02:03:50,210
İhvaz. İhvaz.

1356
02:03:51,920 --> 02:03:55,630
Yours is a life rotten
for a dream.

1357
02:03:57,650 --> 02:04:01,590
We don't rot, weasel.

1358
02:04:03,490 --> 02:04:04,940
Our roots are strong.

1359
02:04:07,610 --> 02:04:11,420
Our branches reach to the sky.

1360
02:04:11,850 --> 02:04:14,940
You are cheated.

1361
02:04:17,080 --> 02:04:20,120
I wish you could be my dog,
just like Barkın.

1362
02:04:41,660 --> 02:04:43,700
Come, Osman.

1363
02:04:45,670 --> 02:04:47,060
Come.

1364
02:05:16,985 --> 02:05:18,695
The traces go this way.

1365
02:05:22,335 --> 02:05:24,345
They must be close.

1366
02:05:25,365 --> 02:05:26,875
Take position.

1367
02:05:27,345 --> 02:05:28,935
Be cautious.

1368
02:05:28,935 --> 02:05:30,455
As you order, my bey.

1369
02:05:41,845 --> 02:05:43,155
Father.

1370
02:05:44,155 --> 02:05:45,545
Father.

1371
02:05:46,025 --> 02:05:47,755
Look, we are here.

1372
02:05:52,925 --> 02:05:54,285
My sheik?

1373
02:05:55,365 --> 02:05:57,435
My sheik is burning, Akça Dervish!

1374
02:05:57,475 --> 02:05:59,065
He is in flames.

1375
02:06:01,135 --> 02:06:03,195
My Allah, help us.

1376
02:06:03,275 --> 02:06:04,615
Kumral Abdal, run!

1377
02:06:04,615 --> 02:06:06,705
Run, Kumral Abdal!

1378
02:06:06,705 --> 02:06:07,965
My sheik is burning!

1379
02:06:07,965 --> 02:06:09,825
Do something1

1380
02:06:09,825 --> 02:06:11,085
Help him!

1381
02:06:11,085 --> 02:06:12,425
My sheik!

1382
02:06:12,425 --> 02:06:13,805
No!

1383
02:06:15,115 --> 02:06:16,685
My Allah!

1384
02:06:16,685 --> 02:06:17,945
Protect him!

1385
02:06:17,945 --> 02:06:20,445
My sheik is poisoned, Bala Hatun.

1386
02:06:20,445 --> 02:06:22,015
He is poisoned!

1387
02:06:23,005 --> 02:06:24,345
Father!

1388
02:06:24,425 --> 02:06:26,165
Father!

1389
02:06:26,365 --> 02:06:27,885
My Allah!

1390
02:06:28,665 --> 02:06:30,405
Father, no!

1391
02:06:36,565 --> 02:06:40,065
Please, please, please!

1392
02:06:41,275 --> 02:06:43,005
No!

1393
02:06:45,565 --> 02:06:47,415
My sheik!

1394
02:07:20,015 --> 02:07:23,045
İnhisar Castle

1395
02:07:23,395 --> 02:07:25,165
Osman Bey should come
on his own.

1396
02:07:25,165 --> 02:07:26,995
He should make his own
demands.

1397
02:07:27,475 --> 02:07:29,675
I'm not feeding his dogs.

1398
02:07:30,545 --> 02:07:32,075
Leave now.

1399
02:07:45,085 --> 02:07:46,855
I explained with words first.

1400
02:07:47,915 --> 02:07:50,485
But if you don't understand from words...

1401
02:07:51,185 --> 02:07:52,755
what do you want?

1402
02:07:54,265 --> 02:07:55,585
Just like this.

1403
02:07:55,665 --> 02:07:58,255
You will pay your taxes to
Osman Bey monthly.

1404
02:07:58,575 --> 02:08:00,585
Or we'll take your castle.

1405
02:08:15,235 --> 02:08:16,745
İrvaz Bey.

1406
02:08:47,335 --> 02:08:49,055
They killed them all.

1407
02:08:49,365 --> 02:08:50,705
All of them.

1408
02:08:52,005 --> 02:08:53,505
İrvaz Bey!

1409
02:08:54,065 --> 02:08:55,635
İrvaz Bey!

1410
02:09:02,175 --> 02:09:03,745
İrvaz Bey!

1411
02:09:12,425 --> 02:09:13,965
Osman.

1412
02:09:21,645 --> 02:09:23,745
İrvaz Bey!

1413
02:09:25,095 --> 02:09:26,345
Who did this!

1414
02:09:40,565 --> 02:09:42,125
İrvaz Bey!

1415
02:09:49,915 --> 02:09:51,415
İrvaz Bey!

1416
02:10:01,845 --> 02:10:03,935
İrvaz is dead.

1417
02:10:12,465 --> 02:10:15,845
You won't live long either.

1418
02:10:18,465 --> 02:10:20,025
You.

1419
02:10:22,335 --> 02:10:23,845
Osman.

1420
02:10:24,615 --> 02:10:29,655
Your light will surrender to my darkness.

1421
02:10:50,905 --> 02:10:56,755
Your darkness will be illuminated
by my sword.

1422
02:11:18,655 --> 02:11:21,655
End of episode 87.

